window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2"]={"id":"CGL-05-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2","title":"CGL 05 OCT 2026 SHIFT 2","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000074381","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, select the related word from the given alternatives.<br>Doctor : Diagnosis :: Judge : ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दिए गए विकल्पों में से संबंधित शब्द चुनिए।<br>Doctor : Diagnosis :: Judge : ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Verdict","hi":"निर्णय"},"2":{"en":"Lawyer","hi":"वकील"},"3":{"en":"Argument","hi":"तर्क"},"4":{"en":"Law","hi":"कानून"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A doctor examines the case and gives a diagnosis<br>In the same way a judge examines the case and gives a verdict ✔<br>A lawyer and an argument are parts of the court process, and law is what the judge follows, so they do not match the relation<br>Hence the answer is Verdict<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Verdict.</b>","hi":"Doctor रोगी की जाँच करके निदान देता है<br>उसी प्रकार Judge मामले की सुनवाई करके निर्णय देता है ✔<br>वकील तथा तर्क न्यायालय की प्रक्रिया के भाग हैं, और कानून वह है जिसका न्यायाधीश पालन करता है, अतः ये संबंध से मेल नहीं खाते<br>इसलिए उत्तर Verdict है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): निर्णय है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000074382","section":"REASONING","topic":"Clock & Calendar","question":{"en":"A seminar was held each day from 11<sup>th</sup> to 18<sup>th</sup> Feb in the following sequence: Raipur, Patna, Jamshedpur, Rourkela, Durgapur, Warangal, Tiruchirappalli, Calicut. How many days after the seminar in Patna did the seminar in Warangal occur? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"11 से 18 फरवरी तक प्रत्येक दिन निम्नलिखित क्रम में सेमिनार हुआ: Raipur, Patna, Jamshedpur, Rourkela, Durgapur, Warangal, Tiruchirappalli, Calicut. Patna के सेमिनार के कितने दिन बाद Warangal का सेमिनार हुआ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 days","hi":"5 दिन"},"2":{"en":"6 days","hi":"6 दिन"},"3":{"en":"3 days","hi":"3 दिन"},"4":{"en":"4 days","hi":"4 दिन"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The first seminar is on 11 Feb at Raipur, so Patna, being second in the list, is on 12 Feb<br>Counting the list, Warangal is the sixth city, so its seminar is on 11 + 5 = 16 Feb<br>The gap is 16 − 12 = 4 days<br>Hence the Warangal seminar was 4 days after the Patna seminar<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4 days.</b>","hi":"पहला सेमिनार 11 फरवरी को Raipur में है, अतः सूची में दूसरे स्थान का Patna 12 फरवरी को है<br>सूची गिनने पर Warangal छठा शहर है, अतः उसका सेमिनार 11 + 5 = 16 फरवरी को है<br>अंतर 16 − 12 = 4 दिन है<br>इसलिए Warangal का सेमिनार Patna के सेमिनार के 4 दिन बाद हुआ<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 4 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000074383","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"If M = 13, O = 15, Q = 17, then S = ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि M = 13, O = 15, Q = 17 है, तो S = ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"19"},"2":{"en":"18"},"3":{"en":"20"},"4":{"en":"21"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Each letter is given the value of its position in the alphabet: M is the 13th letter, O the 15th and Q the 17th ✔<br>S is the 19th letter of the alphabet<br>Hence S = 19<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 19.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को वर्णमाला में उसके स्थान का मान दिया गया है: M 13वाँ, O 15वाँ तथा Q 17वाँ अक्षर है ✔<br>S वर्णमाला का 19वाँ अक्षर है<br>इसलिए S = 19<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 19 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000074384","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"Given in the table are the number codes for the given letters. Select the combination of numbers so that the letters arranged accordingly will form a meaningful word.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">A</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">C</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">R</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">T</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">U</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"तालिका में दिए गए अक्षरों के लिए संख्या कूट दिए गए हैं। संख्याओं का वह संयोजन चुनिए जिससे क्रम में रखे गए अक्षर एक अर्थपूर्ण शब्द बनाएँ।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">A</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">E</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">C</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">R</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">T</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">U</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3, 4, 2, 1, 5, 6, 6, 2"},"2":{"en":"3, 2, 2, 1, 5, 6, 4, 2"},"3":{"en":"3, 4, 2, 1, 5, 6, 4, 2"},"4":{"en":"3, 4, 2, 5, 5, 6, 4, 2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Reading the numbers with their letters gives 3 = C, 4 = R, 2 = E, 1 = A, 5 = T, 6 = U, 4 = R and 2 = E<br>So the letters are C R E A T U R E, which spells the meaningful word CREATURE ✔<br>The other combinations repeat a letter wrongly or place the wrong letter in the middle and do not give a word<br>Hence 3, 4, 2, 1, 5, 6, 4, 2 is the correct combination<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3, 4, 2, 1, 5, 6, 4, 2.</b>","hi":"संख्याओं को उनके अक्षरों के साथ पढ़ने पर 3 = C, 4 = R, 2 = E, 1 = A, 5 = T, 6 = U, 4 = R तथा 2 = E मिलता है<br>अतः अक्षर C R E A T U R E बनते हैं, जो अर्थपूर्ण शब्द CREATURE है ✔<br>अन्य संयोजन किसी अक्षर को गलत रूप से दोहराते हैं या बीच में गलत अक्षर रखते हैं और कोई शब्द नहीं बनाते<br>इसलिए 3, 4, 2, 1, 5, 6, 4, 2 सही संयोजन है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3, 4, 2, 1, 5, 6, 4, 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000074385","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"If the radius of a circle is doubled, what will happen to its area? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि किसी वृत्त की त्रिज्या दोगुनी कर दी जाए, तो उसका क्षेत्रफल क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Double","hi":"दोगुना"},"2":{"en":"Triple","hi":"तीन गुना"},"3":{"en":"Four times","hi":"चार गुना"},"4":{"en":"No change","hi":"कोई परिवर्तन नहीं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The area of a circle is πr²<br>If the radius becomes 2r, the new area is π(2r)² = 4πr²<br>So the area becomes four times the original area<br>Hence the area becomes four times<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Four times.</b>","hi":"वृत्त का क्षेत्रफल πr² है<br>यदि त्रिज्या 2r हो जाए, तो नया क्षेत्रफल π(2r)² = 4πr² है<br>अतः क्षेत्रफल मूल क्षेत्रफल का चार गुना हो जाता है<br>इसलिए क्षेत्रफल चार गुना हो जाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): चार गुना है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000074386","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The average of 5 consecutive odd numbers is 41. What is the largest number? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"5 क्रमागत विषम संख्याओं का औसत 41 है। सबसे बड़ी संख्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"43"},"2":{"en":"45"},"3":{"en":"47"},"4":{"en":"49"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"For consecutive odd numbers the average is the middle number, so the middle number here is 41<br>The five numbers are 37, 39, 41, 43 and 45<br>So the largest number is 45<br>Hence the largest number is 45<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 45.</b>","hi":"क्रमागत विषम संख्याओं का औसत मध्य की संख्या होता है, अतः यहाँ मध्य संख्या 41 है<br>पाँच संख्याएँ 37, 39, 41, 43 तथा 45 हैं<br>अतः सबसे बड़ी संख्या 45 है<br>इसलिए सबसे बड़ी संख्या 45 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 45 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000074387","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What comes next: 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अगली संख्या क्या है: 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"13"},"2":{"en":"12"},"3":{"en":"11"},"4":{"en":"14"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Every term is the sum of the two terms before it: 0 + 1 = 1, 1 + 1 = 2, 1 + 2 = 3, 2 + 3 = 5 and 3 + 5 = 8 ✔<br>So the next term is 5 + 8 = 13<br>Hence the next number is 13<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 13.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद अपने पहले के दो पदों का योग है: 0 + 1 = 1, 1 + 1 = 2, 1 + 2 = 3, 2 + 3 = 5 तथा 3 + 5 = 8 ✔<br>अतः अगला पद 5 + 8 = 13 है<br>इसलिए अगली संख्या 13 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 13 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000074388","section":"REASONING","topic":"Seating & Mixed Arrangement","question":{"en":"Direction: Read the given information carefully and answer the given question.<br>Eight persons S, T, U, V, W, X, Y and Z live in an eight storey building such that ground floor is numbered as 1 and the top floor is numbered as 8. X lives on an even numbered floor below the floor number 6. More than two persons live between X and S. S does not live on an odd numbered floor. The number of persons living above S is the same as the number of persons living below V. Two people live between Y and T. T lives just above X. Only one person lives between U and Z. Z lives on one of the floors above Y.<br>Who among the following lives just below W? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निर्देश: दी गई जानकारी ध्यान से पढ़िए और दिए गए प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br>आठ व्यक्ति S, T, U, V, W, X, Y तथा Z आठ मंजिला इमारत में रहते हैं, जहाँ भूतल 1 तथा सबसे ऊपरी मंजिल 8 है। X मंजिल संख्या 6 से नीचे किसी सम संख्या वाली मंजिल पर रहता है। X और S के बीच दो से अधिक व्यक्ति रहते हैं। S किसी विषम संख्या वाली मंजिल पर नहीं रहता। S के ऊपर रहने वाले व्यक्तियों की संख्या V के नीचे रहने वाले व्यक्तियों की संख्या के बराबर है। Y और T के बीच दो व्यक्ति रहते हैं। T, X के ठीक ऊपर रहता है। U और Z के बीच केवल एक व्यक्ति रहता है। Z, Y से ऊपर किसी मंजिल पर रहता है।<br>निम्न में से कौन W के ठीक नीचे रहता है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"X"},"2":{"en":"T"},"3":{"en":"Z"},"4":{"en":"U"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"X is on an even floor below 6, so X can be on 2 or 4, and T lives just above X<br>More than two persons are between X and S with S above X, and S is on an even floor: this puts X on floor 2 and S on floor 8<br>The persons above S are none, so V must have none below, which puts V on floor 1<br>Two people between Y and T with Z above Y gives Y on floor 6, Z on floor 7, and U on floor 5 with one person between U and Z ✔<br>The floors are V-1, X-2, T-3, W-4, U-5, Y-6, Z-7 and S-8, so T lives just below W<br>Hence T lives just below W<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): T.</b>","hi":"X, 6 से नीचे सम संख्या वाली मंजिल पर है, अतः X मंजिल 2 या 4 पर हो सकता है, और T, X के ठीक ऊपर रहता है<br>X और S के बीच दो से अधिक व्यक्ति हैं तथा S, X के ऊपर सम मंजिल पर है: इससे X मंजिल 2 पर और S मंजिल 8 पर तय होता है<br>S के ऊपर कोई नहीं है, अतः V के नीचे भी कोई नहीं होगा, जिससे V मंजिल 1 पर आता है<br>Y और T के बीच दो व्यक्ति तथा Z, Y के ऊपर होने से Y मंजिल 6 पर, Z मंजिल 7 पर तथा U मंजिल 5 पर आता है, U और Z के बीच एक व्यक्ति के साथ ✔<br>मंजिलें हैं V-1, X-2, T-3, W-4, U-5, Y-6, Z-7 तथा S-8, अतः T, W के ठीक नीचे रहता है<br>इसलिए T, W के ठीक नीचे रहता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): T है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000074389","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the following statement carefully and identify the conclusion that follows.<br><b>Statement:</b> The bank has announced a 0% interest loan scheme for students.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Students will be encouraged to pursue higher education.<br>II. The bank is not concerned about making profits. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और वह निष्कर्ष पहचानिए जो निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b> बैंक ने विद्यार्थियों के लिए 0% ब्याज ऋण योजना की घोषणा की है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. विद्यार्थी उच्च शिक्षा प्राप्त करने के लिए प्रोत्साहित होंगे।<br>II. बैंक लाभ कमाने की चिंता नहीं करता। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both I and II follow","hi":"I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither I nor II follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A loan scheme without interest makes higher education cheaper for students, so it will encourage them to study further and conclusion I follows ✔<br>Charging no interest on one scheme does not mean that the bank has no interest in profits, so conclusion II is too wide ✘<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I follows.</b>","hi":"बिना ब्याज की ऋण योजना विद्यार्थियों के लिए उच्च शिक्षा सस्ती बनाती है, अतः वे आगे पढ़ने के लिए प्रोत्साहित होंगे और निष्कर्ष I निकलता है ✔<br>एक योजना पर ब्याज न लेना यह नहीं दर्शाता कि बैंक लाभ की चिंता नहीं करता, अतः निष्कर्ष II अत्यधिक व्यापक है ✘<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000074390","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Analogy","question":{"en":"Find the number that best completes the analogy. E : 40 :: K : ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वह संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए जो सादृश्य पूरा करती है। E : 40 :: K : ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"88"},"2":{"en":"90"},"3":{"en":"86"},"4":{"en":"78"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The position of E in the alphabet is 5, and 5 × 8 = 40 ✔<br>The position of K is 11, so the matching number is 11 × 8 = 88<br>Hence the answer is 88<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 88.</b>","hi":"वर्णमाला में E का स्थान 5 है और 5 × 8 = 40 ✔<br>K का स्थान 11 है, अतः संबंधित संख्या 11 × 8 = 88 है<br>इसलिए उत्तर 88 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 88 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000074391","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Choose the correct option to complete the series.<br>Microscope : Magnify :: Speaker : ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"श्रेणी पूरी करने के लिए सही विकल्प चुनिए।<br>Microscope : Magnify :: Speaker : ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Listen","hi":"सुनना"},"2":{"en":"Reduce","hi":"घटाना"},"3":{"en":"Quiet","hi":"शांत"},"4":{"en":"Amplify","hi":"बढ़ाना (ध्वनि)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A microscope is a device used to magnify things<br>In the same way a speaker is a device used to amplify sound ✔<br>Listening is done by a person, reducing and quiet are not functions of a speaker<br>Hence the answer is Amplify<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Amplify.</b>","hi":"सूक्ष्मदर्शी वह उपकरण है जो वस्तुओं को बड़ा करके दिखाता है<br>उसी प्रकार स्पीकर वह उपकरण है जो ध्वनि को बढ़ाता है ✔<br>सुनना व्यक्ति करता है, और घटाना तथा शांत स्पीकर के कार्य नहीं हैं<br>इसलिए उत्तर Amplify है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): बढ़ाना (ध्वनि) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000074392","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Select the letter cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series.<br>GDR, CHN, YLI, ?, QTB [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए विकल्पों में से वह अक्षर-समूह चुनिए जो निम्नलिखित श्रेणी में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर आ सके।<br>GDR, CHN, YLI, ?, QTB [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"UPF"},"2":{"en":"UDH"},"3":{"en":"VPE"},"4":{"en":"VMF"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The first letters G, C, Y, U, Q move four places back at every step ✔<br>The second letters D, H, L, P, T move four places ahead at every step ✔<br>The third letters are R, N, I, ?, B, and the printed key cluster has P at the third place, so the third letters do not follow one uniform step<br>SSC has given this answer in the official answer key, so the key value UPF is kept<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): UPF.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर G, C, Y, U, Q प्रत्येक चरण में चार स्थान पीछे जाते हैं ✔<br>दूसरे अक्षर D, H, L, P, T प्रत्येक चरण में चार स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं ✔<br>तीसरे अक्षर R, N, I, ?, B हैं और कुंजी वाले समूह में तीसरे स्थान पर P है, अतः तीसरे अक्षर कोई एक समान चरण नहीं दर्शाते<br>SSC ने आधिकारिक उत्तर कुंजी में यही उत्तर दिया है, अतः कुंजी का मान UPF ही रखा गया है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): UPF है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000074393","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What is the 8th term of the series?<br>2, 6, 10, 14, ...? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"श्रेणी का 8वाँ पद क्या है?<br>2, 6, 10, 14, ...? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"26"},"2":{"en":"28"},"3":{"en":"30"},"4":{"en":"32"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The first term is a = 2 and the common difference is d = 4<br>The nth term is a + (n − 1)d, so the 8th term is 2 + 7 × 4 = 2 + 28 = 30<br>Hence the 8th term is 30<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 30.</b>","hi":"पहला पद a = 2 तथा सार्व अंतर d = 4 है<br>nवाँ पद a + (n − 1)d है, अतः 8वाँ पद 2 + 7 × 4 = 2 + 28 = 30 है<br>इसलिए 8वाँ पद 30 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 30 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000074394","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If POCKET is coded as QPDLFU, how is QPDLFU coded? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि POCKET का कूट QPDLFU है, तो QPDLFU का कूट क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RQEMGV"},"2":{"en":"RQEMFU"},"3":{"en":"RPDMGV"},"4":{"en":"RPEMGV"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In POCKET every letter moves one place ahead: P→Q, O→P, C→D, K→L, E→F and T→U, which gives QPDLFU ✔<br>Applying the same step to QPDLFU: Q→R, P→Q, D→E, L→M, F→G and U→V<br>Hence QPDLFU is coded as RQEMGV<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): RQEMGV.</b>","hi":"POCKET में प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान आगे जाता है: P→Q, O→P, C→D, K→L, E→F तथा T→U, जिससे QPDLFU मिलता है ✔<br>QPDLFU पर वही चरण लगाने से Q→R, P→Q, D→E, L→M, F→G तथा U→V<br>इसलिए QPDLFU का कूट RQEMGV है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): RQEMGV है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000074395","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"INTERNATIONAL\" is written as \"IOTFROAUIPNBL\". How will \"COMMUNICATION\" be written? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"INTERNATIONAL\" को \"IOTFROAUIPNBL\" लिखा जाता है। \"COMMUNICATION\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"CPMNUOIDAUIPN"},"2":{"en":"CPNMUOIDUAIPN"},"3":{"en":"CPMNIUODIUAPN"},"4":{"en":"CPMUNODIAUIPN"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Comparing INTERNATIONAL with IOTFROAUIPNBL shows that the letters in the odd places stay the same while the letters in the even places move one place ahead: I same, N→O, T same, E→F, R same, N→O, A same, T→U, I same, O→P, N same, A→B and L same ✔<br>Applying the same step to COMMUNICATION: C same, O→P, M same, M→N, U same, N→O, I same, C→D, A same, T→U, I same, O→P and N same<br>Hence COMMUNICATION is written as CPMNUOIDAUIPN<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): CPMNUOIDAUIPN.</b>","hi":"INTERNATIONAL तथा IOTFROAUIPNBL की तुलना से दिखता है कि विषम स्थानों के अक्षर वही रहते हैं जबकि सम स्थानों के अक्षर एक स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं: I वैसा, N→O, T वैसा, E→F, R वैसा, N→O, A वैसा, T→U, I वैसा, O→P, N वैसा, A→B तथा L वैसा ✔<br>COMMUNICATION पर वही चरण लगाने से C वैसा, O→P, M वैसा, M→N, U वैसा, N→O, I वैसा, C→D, A वैसा, T→U, I वैसा, O→P तथा N वैसा<br>इसलिए COMMUNICATION को CPMNUOIDAUIPN लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): CPMNUOIDAUIPN है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000074396","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"If in the word EDUCATION the first and second letters are interchanged, in the same way the third and fourth, fifth and sixth and so on are interchanged, then what will be the 5th letter from the right? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि शब्द EDUCATION में पहले और दूसरे अक्षर को परस्पर बदला जाए, उसी प्रकार तीसरे और चौथे, पाँचवें और छठे और इसी तरह आगे भी बदला जाए, तो दाएँ से पाँचवाँ अक्षर क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"U"},"2":{"en":"C"},"3":{"en":"T"},"4":{"en":"E"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Swapping the letters in pairs turns EDUCATION into D E C U T A O I N<br>Counting from the right, the letters are N, I, O, A and T<br>So the 5th letter from the right is T<br>Hence the answer is T<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): T.</b>","hi":"जोड़ों में अक्षर बदलने से EDUCATION बनता है D E C U T A O I N<br>दाएँ से गिनने पर अक्षर N, I, O, A तथा T हैं<br>अतः दाएँ से पाँचवाँ अक्षर T है<br>इसलिए उत्तर T है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): T है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000074397","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"How many letters will remain at the same position in the word 'TEACHING' when the letters are arranged in reverse English alphabetical order from left to right? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"शब्द 'TEACHING' के अक्षरों को बाएँ से दाएँ अंग्रेज़ी वर्णमाला के उल्टे क्रम में व्यवस्थित करने पर कितने अक्षर अपने स्थान पर ही रहेंगे? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"TEACHING has the letters T, E, A, C, H, I, N and G, whose reverse alphabetical order is T, N, I, H, G, E, C and A<br>Comparing place by place, only the first letter T keeps its position, as E→N, A→I, C→H, H→G, I→E, N→C and G→A<br>Hence 1 letter remains at the same position<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"TEACHING में अक्षर T, E, A, C, H, I, N तथा G हैं, जिनका उल्टा वर्णमाला क्रम T, N, I, H, G, E, C तथा A है<br>स्थान-दर-स्थान तुलना करने पर केवल पहला अक्षर T अपने स्थान पर रहता है, क्योंकि E→N, A→I, C→H, H→G, I→E, N→C तथा G→A<br>इसलिए 1 अक्षर अपने स्थान पर रहता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000074398","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">19</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। यह पैटर्न पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">19</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"11"},"2":{"en":"19"},"3":{"en":"23"},"4":{"en":"31"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In every row the third number is the product of the first two numbers minus their sum<br>First row: 6 × 5 − (6 + 5) = 30 − 11 = 19 ✔ and second row: 8 × 2 − (8 + 2) = 16 − 10 = 6 ✔<br>Third row: 9 × 4 − (9 + 4) = 36 − 13 = 23<br>Hence the missing number is 23<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 23.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में तीसरी संख्या पहली दो संख्याओं के गुणनफल में से उनका योग घटाने पर मिलती है<br>पहली पंक्ति: 6 × 5 − (6 + 5) = 30 − 11 = 19 ✔ तथा दूसरी पंक्ति: 8 × 2 − (8 + 2) = 16 − 10 = 6 ✔<br>तीसरी पंक्ति: 9 × 4 − (9 + 4) = 36 − 13 = 23<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 23 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 23 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000074399","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"In a coded family relationship system:<br>P @ Q indicates that P is the mother of Q.<br>P # Q indicates that P is the father of Q.<br>P &#36; Q indicates that P is the brother of Q.<br>P % Q indicates that P is the sister of Q.<br>Which of the following expressions indicates that M is the maternal uncle of R? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक कूट परिवार संबंध प्रणाली में:<br>P @ Q का अर्थ है P, Q की माता है।<br>P # Q का अर्थ है P, Q का पिता है।<br>P &#36; Q का अर्थ है P, Q का भाई है।<br>P % Q का अर्थ है P, Q की बहन है।<br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा व्यंजक दर्शाता है कि M, R का मामा है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"M &#36; S @ R"},"2":{"en":"M % S @ R"},"3":{"en":"M # S &#36; R"},"4":{"en":"M &#36; S # R"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"For M to be the maternal uncle of R, M must be the brother of R's mother<br>In M &#36; S @ R, M is the brother of S and S is the mother of R, so M is the brother of R's mother ✔<br>M % S @ R makes M the sister of R's mother, and the third and fourth options make M the father or the brother of R's father, which are not maternal uncle<br>Hence M &#36; S @ R is the correct expression<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): M &#36; S @ R.</b>","hi":"M के R का मामा होने के लिए M, R की माता का भाई होना चाहिए<br>M &#36; S @ R में M, S का भाई है और S, R की माता है, अतः M, R की माता का भाई है ✔<br>M % S @ R में M, R की माता की बहन है, तथा तीसरा और चौथा विकल्प M को R के पिता या पिता का भाई बनाते हैं, जो मामा नहीं है<br>इसलिए M &#36; S @ R सही व्यंजक है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): M &#36; S @ R है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000074400","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Select the odd number pair from the given alternatives. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए विकल्पों में से विषम संख्या-युग्म चुनिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"28, 816"},"2":{"en":"37, 1406"},"3":{"en":"51, 2652"},"4":{"en":"64, 4160"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the second pair 37 × 38 = 1406 ✔, in the third 51 × 52 = 2652 ✔ and in the fourth 64 × 65 = 4160 ✔<br>In the first pair 28 × 29 = 812, but the pair shows 816 ✘<br>Hence 28, 816 is the odd pair<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 28, 816.</b>","hi":"दूसरे युग्म में 37 × 38 = 1406 ✔, तीसरे में 51 × 52 = 2652 ✔ तथा चौथे में 64 × 65 = 4160 ✔<br>पहले युग्म में 28 × 29 = 812 है, परंतु युग्म में 816 है ✘<br>इसलिए 28, 816 विषम युग्म है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 28, 816 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000074401","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Due to a sudden corporate merger, your senior role is eliminated. You are offered a choice: take a 30% salary cut and report directly to a manager who is ten years younger than you and has far less field experience or leave the firm tomorrow without another job lined up. You feel an intense wave of public shame. Which reaction shows the highest level of emotional resilience? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अचानक कॉर्पोरेट विलय के कारण आपकी वरिष्ठ भूमिका समाप्त कर दी जाती है। आपको विकल्प दिया जाता है: 30% वेतन कटौती स्वीकार करके ऐसे प्रबंधक को रिपोर्ट करना जो आपसे दस वर्ष छोटा है और जिसका क्षेत्रीय अनुभव बहुत कम है, या बिना दूसरी नौकरी के कल फर्म छोड़ देना। आप सार्वजनिक अपमान की तीव्र भावना महसूस करते हैं। कौन-सी प्रतिक्रिया भावनात्मक लचीलेपन का उच्चतम स्तर दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Resign instantly on the spot to protect your self-respect, regardless of your personal home loan liabilities.","hi":"अपने आत्म-सम्मान की रक्षा के लिए, व्यक्तिगत गृह ऋण देनदारियों की परवाह किए बिना, वहीं तुरंत इस्तीफ़ा दे देना।"},"2":{"en":"Force yourself to feel completely happy and enthusiastic about reporting to the younger manager to prove you have a positive corporate attitude.","hi":"यह सिद्ध करने के लिए कि आपका कॉर्पोरेट दृष्टिकोण सकारात्मक है, कम उम्र के प्रबंधक को रिपोर्ट करने पर स्वयं को पूरी तरह खुश और उत्साही महसूस करने के लिए विवश करना।"},"3":{"en":"Accept the role quietly to stay financially secure, process your feelings privately, and use the frustration to pursue external senior opportunities.","hi":"आर्थिक रूप से सुरक्षित रहने के लिए भूमिका चुपचाप स्वीकार करना, अपनी भावनाओं को निजी रूप से संभालना और उस निराशा का उपयोग बाहर वरिष्ठ अवसर खोजने में करना।"},"4":{"en":"Accept the role, but quietly spread negative gossip about the new manager's lack of experience to protect your reputation among peers.","hi":"भूमिका स्वीकार करना, परंतु साथियों में अपनी प्रतिष्ठा बचाने के लिए नए प्रबंधक के कम अनुभव के बारे में चुपचाप नकारात्मक गपशप फैलाना।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Resilience means staying steady under a blow and choosing the step that protects both the family and the career<br>Accepting the role keeps the income safe, handling the hurt privately protects dignity, and using the frustration to look for senior roles outside turns the setback into action<br>Resigning at once harms the family finances, forcing fake happiness hides the real feeling, and gossip damages the team and your own credibility<br>Hence accepting quietly, processing privately and pursuing senior opportunities externally shows the highest emotional resilience<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Accept the role quietly to stay financially secure, process your feelings privately, and use the frustration to pursue external senior opportunities..</b>","hi":"लचीलापन का अर्थ है आघात के समय स्थिर रहना और ऐसा कदम चुनना जो परिवार तथा करियर दोनों की रक्षा करे<br>भूमिका स्वीकार करना आय सुरक्षित रखता है, चोट को निजी रूप से संभालना गरिमा बचाता है, और निराशा का उपयोग बाहर वरिष्ठ अवसर खोजने में करना असफलता को कर्म में बदल देता है<br>तुरंत इस्तीफ़ा परिवार की आर्थिक स्थिति को हानि पहुँचाता है, नकली खुशी दिखाना वास्तविक भावना छिपाता है, और गपशप टीम तथा आपकी विश्वसनीयता दोनों को हानि पहुँचाती है<br>अतः चुपचाप स्वीकार करना, भावनाएँ निजी रूप से संभालना तथा बाहर वरिष्ठ अवसर खोजना भावनात्मक लचीलेपन का उच्चतम स्तर दर्शाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): आर्थिक रूप से सुरक्षित रहने के लिए भूमिका चुपचाप स्वीकार करना, अपनी भावनाओं को निजी रूप से संभालना और उस निराशा का उपयोग बाहर वरिष्ठ अवसर खोजने में करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000074402","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The Civil Tribunal has appealed to the citizens for cooperation to prevent blatant theft of power in the area.<br><b>Conclusion:</b><br>I. Local civic groups will respond to this request by forming teams of people to investigate such power issues.<br>II. Those who steal power will stop stealing power due to fear of rebuke from society. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सिविल न्यायाधिकरण ने क्षेत्र में बिजली की खुली चोरी रोकने के लिए नागरिकों से सहयोग की अपील की है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. स्थानीय नागरिक समूह इस अनुरोध पर ऐसी बिजली समस्याओं की जाँच के लिए लोगों की टीमें बनाकर प्रतिक्रिया देंगे।<br>II. बिजली चोरी करने वाले समाज की भर्त्सना के डर से चोरी करना बंद कर देंगे। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither Conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement only makes an appeal for cooperation and does not say what the civic groups will actually do, so conclusion I is not certain<br>It also does not say that the thieves will change their behaviour, so conclusion II is not certain either<br>Hence neither conclusion I nor II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither Conclusion I nor II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन केवल सहयोग की अपील करता है और यह नहीं कहता कि नागरिक समूह वास्तव में क्या करेंगे, अतः निष्कर्ष I निश्चित नहीं है<br>यह यह भी नहीं कहता कि चोर अपना व्यवहार बदल देंगे, अतः निष्कर्ष II भी निश्चित नहीं है<br>इसलिए न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000074403","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"A florist specialises in grand wedding arrangements, which creates irregular demand. She wants to ensure her shop remains profitable and busy on a standard workday. What should she implement? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक फूलविक्रेता भव्य विवाह व्यवस्थाओं में विशेषज्ञता रखती है, जिससे माँग अनियमित रहती है। वह चाहती है कि उसकी दुकान सामान्य कार्यदिवस पर भी लाभदायक और व्यस्त रहे। उसे क्या लागू करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Launching a weekly subscription service for small home bouquets.","hi":"छोटे घरेलू गुलदस्तों के लिए साप्ताहिक सदस्यता सेवा शुरू करना।"},"2":{"en":"Targeting only luxury event planners for massive gala projects.","hi":"विशाल गाला परियोजनाओं के लिए केवल लक्ज़री इवेंट प्लानरों को लक्षित करना।"},"3":{"en":"Stocking only rare exotic flowers imported from other nations.","hi":"केवल दूसरे देशों से आयातित दुर्लभ विदेशी फूल रखना।"},"4":{"en":"Renovating the storefront to look like an upscale wedding hall.","hi":"दुकान के अग्रभाग को उच्च-स्तरीय विवाह हॉल जैसा दिखाने के लिए नवीनीकृत करना।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The problem is irregular demand, so the cure is a steady, repeat source of small orders<br>A weekly subscription for small home bouquets brings regular customers on ordinary days and keeps the shop busy and profitable ✔<br>Targeting only luxury planners keeps the demand as irregular as before, stocking only rare imported flowers raises costs without adding regular buyers, and renovating the front does not create daily sales<br>Hence launching a weekly subscription service for small home bouquets is the right step<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Launching a weekly subscription service for small home bouquets..</b>","hi":"समस्या अनियमित माँग है, अतः उपाय छोटे ऑर्डरों का स्थिर और दोहराया जाने वाला स्रोत है<br>छोटे घरेलू गुलदस्तों के लिए साप्ताहिक सदस्यता सेवा सामान्य दिनों में नियमित ग्राहक लाती है और दुकान को व्यस्त तथा लाभदायक रखती है ✔<br>केवल लक्ज़री प्लानरों को लक्षित करने से माँग पहले जैसी अनियमित रहती है, केवल दुर्लभ आयातित फूल रखने से लागत बढ़ती है पर नियमित खरीदार नहीं, और अग्रभाग का नवीनीकरण दैनिक बिक्री नहीं देता<br>अतः छोटे घरेलू गुलदस्तों के लिए साप्ताहिक सदस्यता सेवा शुरू करना सही कदम है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): छोटे घरेलू गुलदस्तों के लिए साप्ताहिक सदस्यता सेवा शुरू करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000074404","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>To combat the rising threat of cybercrime, the government must pass legislation requiring all online service providers to implement multi-factor authentication for every user account.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Multi-factor authentication is a reliable method for enhancing the security of digital user accounts.<br>II. Current security measures employed by service providers are insufficient to stop cybercriminals. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिया गया कथन तथा उस पर आधारित अवधारणाएँ ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सी अवधारणाएँ कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>बढ़ते साइबर अपराध के खतरे से निपटने के लिए सरकार को ऐसा कानून बनाना चाहिए जो सभी ऑनलाइन सेवा प्रदाताओं के लिए प्रत्येक उपयोगकर्ता खाते पर बहु-कारक प्रमाणीकरण अनिवार्य करे।<br><b>अवधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. बहु-कारक प्रमाणीकरण डिजिटल उपयोगकर्ता खातों की सुरक्षा बढ़ाने का विश्वसनीय तरीका है।<br>II. सेवा प्रदाताओं द्वारा प्रयुक्त वर्तमान सुरक्षा उपाय साइबर अपराधियों को रोकने के लिए अपर्याप्त हैं। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा II निहित है"},"3":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अवधारणा I और न ही II निहित है"},"4":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अवधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A law making multi-factor authentication compulsory is proposed only because such authentication is believed to strengthen account security, so assumption I is implicit ✔<br>The very need to add a new safeguard shows that the present measures are taken to be insufficient against cybercriminals, so assumption II is also implicit ✔<br>Hence both assumptions I and II are implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Both Assumptions I and II are implicit.</b>","hi":"बहु-कारक प्रमाणीकरण अनिवार्य करने वाला कानून इसलिए प्रस्तावित है क्योंकि ऐसा प्रमाणीकरण खाता सुरक्षा मजबूत करता माना जाता है, अतः अवधारणा I निहित है ✔<br>नया सुरक्षा उपाय जोड़ने की आवश्यकता ही यह दर्शाती है कि वर्तमान उपाय साइबर अपराधियों के विरुद्ध अपर्याप्त माने जाते हैं, अतः अवधारणा II भी निहित है ✔<br>इसलिए अवधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): अवधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000074405","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Select the group of letters that is different from the other three. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उस अक्षर-समूह का चयन कीजिए जो अन्य तीन से भिन्न है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ACEG"},"2":{"en":"BDFH"},"3":{"en":"CEGI"},"4":{"en":"DFIK"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In ACEG each letter is two places ahead of the one before; BDFH and CEGI follow the same step of +2 ✔<br>In DFIK the steps are D→F (+2), F→I (+3) and I→K (+2), so the group does not keep the same gap<br>Hence DFIK is different from the other three<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): DFIK.</b>","hi":"ACEG में प्रत्येक अक्षर अपने पहले अक्षर से दो स्थान आगे है; BDFH तथा CEGI भी +2 का ही पालन करते हैं ✔<br>DFIK में चरण D→F (+2), F→I (+3) तथा I→K (+2) हैं, अतः समूह वही अंतर नहीं रखता<br>इसलिए DFIK अन्य तीन से भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): DFIK है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000074406","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Reports and Indices (Current)","question":{"en":"What is the typical rating scale used in the Gallup survey for happiness? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"प्रसन्नता के लिए गैलप सर्वेक्षण में सामान्यतः किस रेटिंग पैमाने का उपयोग किया जाता है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 to 5","hi":"1 से 5"},"2":{"en":"0 to 100","hi":"0 से 100"},"3":{"en":"0 to 10","hi":"0 से 10"},"4":{"en":"1 to 20","hi":"1 से 20"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 0 to 10</b><br>The Gallup World Poll uses the <b>Cantril Ladder</b>, where respondents rate their current life on a scale of <b><u>0 to 10</u></b> – 0 being the worst possible life and 10 the best possible life.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• This scale is the basis of the <b>World Happiness Report</b>, published since <b>2012</b>.<br>• The six factors used to explain scores: <b>GDP per capita, social support, healthy life expectancy, freedom, generosity and perceptions of corruption</b>.<br>• <b>Finland</b> has topped the report for several consecutive years.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 0 से 10</b><br>गैलप वर्ल्ड पोल <b>कैंट्रिल सीढ़ी (Cantril Ladder)</b> का उपयोग करता है, जिसमें उत्तरदाता अपने वर्तमान जीवन को <b><u>0 से 10</u></b> के पैमाने पर आँकते हैं – 0 सबसे खराब और 10 सबसे अच्छा संभव जीवन।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यही पैमाना <b>विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट</b> का आधार है, जो <b>2012</b> से प्रकाशित हो रही है।<br>• अंकों को समझाने वाले छह कारक: <b>प्रति व्यक्ति GDP, सामाजिक सहयोग, स्वस्थ जीवन प्रत्याशा, स्वतंत्रता, उदारता और भ्रष्टाचार की धारणा</b>।<br>• <b>फ़िनलैंड</b> लगातार कई वर्षों से रिपोर्ट में शीर्ष पर है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000074407","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"What is the name of the system that provides location-specific air quality and weather forecasting? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"स्थान-विशिष्ट वायु गुणवत्ता और मौसम पूर्वानुमान प्रदान करने वाली प्रणाली का नाम क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"NAMASTE","hi":"नमस्ते"},"2":{"en":"SAFAR","hi":"सफ़र"},"3":{"en":"VARSHA","hi":"वर्षा"},"4":{"en":"MAUSAM","hi":"मौसम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – SAFAR</b><br><b><u>SAFAR</u></b> – <b>System of Air Quality and Weather Forecasting And Research</b> – gives location-specific air quality and weather forecasts for major Indian cities.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Developed by the <b>Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology (IITM), Pune</b> under the <b>Ministry of Earth Sciences</b>.<br>• First launched for <b>Delhi</b> during the <b>Commonwealth Games 2010</b>.<br>• It measures pollutants such as PM2.5, PM10, ozone, CO and NOx, along with UV index.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सफ़र</b><br><b><u>सफ़र (SAFAR)</u></b> – <b>वायु गुणवत्ता और मौसम पूर्वानुमान तथा अनुसंधान प्रणाली (System of Air Quality and Weather Forecasting And Research)</b> – प्रमुख भारतीय शहरों के लिए स्थान-विशिष्ट वायु गुणवत्ता और मौसम पूर्वानुमान देती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>पृथ्वी विज्ञान मंत्रालय</b> के अधीन <b>भारतीय उष्णकटिबंधीय मौसम विज्ञान संस्थान (IITM), पुणे</b> द्वारा विकसित।<br>• पहली बार <b>राष्ट्रमंडल खेल 2010</b> के दौरान <b>दिल्ली</b> के लिए शुरू।<br>• यह PM2.5, PM10, ओज़ोन, CO और NOx जैसे प्रदूषकों के साथ UV सूचकांक भी मापती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000074408","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"What is a key difficulty in establishing efficient Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) processes to boost business operations in regions with fragile legal systems? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कमज़ोर विधिक प्रणालियों वाले क्षेत्रों में व्यावसायिक गतिविधियों को बढ़ावा देने हेतु कुशल वैकल्पिक विवाद समाधान (ADR) प्रक्रियाएँ स्थापित करने में एक प्रमुख कठिनाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Limited access to experienced ADR professionals and problems with enforcing arbitration rulings.","hi":"अनुभवी ADR पेशेवरों तक सीमित पहुँच और मध्यस्थता निर्णयों को लागू करने में समस्याएँ।"},"2":{"en":"Strong dependence on traditional court systems for resolving trade-related disputes.","hi":"व्यापार-संबंधी विवादों के समाधान के लिए पारंपरिक न्यायालय प्रणाली पर अधिक निर्भरता।"},"3":{"en":"Extensive use of common international arbitration standards.","hi":"सामान्य अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मध्यस्थता मानकों का व्यापक उपयोग।"},"4":{"en":"Widespread reliance on informal methods of conflict resolution.","hi":"संघर्ष समाधान के अनौपचारिक तरीकों पर व्यापक निर्भरता।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Limited access to experienced ADR professionals and problems with enforcing arbitration rulings.</b><br>Where legal systems are weak, ADR suffers from a <b><u>shortage of trained arbitrators/mediators</u></b> and <b><u>difficulty in enforcing arbitral awards</u></b>, because enforcement finally depends on courts.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• ADR methods: <b>Arbitration, Mediation, Conciliation, Negotiation and Lok Adalat</b>.<br>• India's law: <b>Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996</b>; <b>Mediation Act, 2023</b>.<br>• <b>Section 89 of the CPC</b> provides for referral of disputes to ADR; Lok Adalats work under the <b>Legal Services Authorities Act, 1987</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अनुभवी ADR पेशेवरों तक सीमित पहुँच और मध्यस्थता निर्णयों को लागू करने में समस्याएँ।</b><br>जहाँ विधिक प्रणालियाँ कमज़ोर होती हैं, वहाँ ADR <b><u>प्रशिक्षित मध्यस्थों की कमी</u></b> और <b><u>मध्यस्थता निर्णयों (Arbitral awards) को लागू करने में कठिनाई</u></b> से प्रभावित होता है, क्योंकि प्रवर्तन अंततः न्यायालयों पर निर्भर करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ADR पद्धतियाँ: <b>मध्यस्थता (Arbitration), मध्यस्थ-सुलह (Mediation), सुलह (Conciliation), बातचीत और लोक अदालत</b>।<br>• भारत का कानून: <b>मध्यस्थता और सुलह अधिनियम, 1996</b>; <b>मध्यस्थता अधिनियम, 2023</b>।<br>• <b>CPC की धारा 89</b> विवादों को ADR को सौंपने का प्रावधान करती है; लोक अदालतें <b>विधिक सेवा प्राधिकरण अधिनियम, 1987</b> के तहत कार्य करती हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000074409","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"__________ known as the \"Rocket Woman of India\", played a key role as the Deputy Operations Director of Mangalyaan. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"__________ जिन्हें \"भारत की रॉकेट वुमन\" के रूप में जाना जाता है, ने मंगलयान की डिप्टी ऑपरेशंस डायरेक्टर के रूप में महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका निभाई। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ritu Karidhal","hi":"ऋतु करिधाल"},"2":{"en":"K. Sivan","hi":"के. सिवन"},"3":{"en":"Kalpana Chawla","hi":"कल्पना चावला"},"4":{"en":"Tessy Thomas","hi":"टेसी थॉमस"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Ritu Karidhal</b><br>ISRO scientist <b><u>Ritu Karidhal</u></b>, called the <b>\"Rocket Woman of India\"</b>, was the <b>Deputy Operations Director of the Mars Orbiter Mission (Mangalyaan)</b> and later Mission Director of Chandrayaan-2.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Mangalyaan was launched on <b>5 November 2013</b> by <b>PSLV-C25</b>; it entered Mars orbit on <b>24 September 2014</b>.<br>• India became the <b>first country to reach Mars orbit in its first attempt</b>.<br>• <b>Tessy Thomas</b> is called the <b>\"Missile Woman of India\"</b> (Agni project).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – ऋतु करिधाल</b><br>ISRO वैज्ञानिक <b><u>ऋतु करिधाल</u></b>, जिन्हें <b>\"भारत की रॉकेट वुमन\"</b> कहा जाता है, <b>मंगल कक्षित्र मिशन (मंगलयान)</b> की <b>डिप्टी ऑपरेशंस डायरेक्टर</b> थीं और बाद में चंद्रयान-2 की मिशन डायरेक्टर बनीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मंगलयान <b>5 नवंबर 2013</b> को <b>PSLV-C25</b> से प्रक्षेपित हुआ; यह <b>24 सितंबर 2014</b> को मंगल की कक्षा में पहुँचा।<br>• भारत <b>पहले प्रयास में मंगल की कक्षा तक पहुँचने वाला पहला देश</b> बना।<br>• <b>टेसी थॉमस</b> को <b>\"भारत की मिसाइल वुमन\"</b> (अग्नि परियोजना) कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000074410","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Which of the following reflects a social impact of ISRO’s satellite technology in India? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा भारत में ISRO की उपग्रह प्रौद्योगिकी के सामाजिक प्रभाव को दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Study of black holes","hi":"ब्लैक होल का अध्ययन"},"2":{"en":"Deep space exploration","hi":"गहन अंतरिक्ष अन्वेषण"},"3":{"en":"Improved remote education in rural areas","hi":"ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों में बेहतर दूरस्थ शिक्षा"},"4":{"en":"Discovery of exoplanets","hi":"बाह्यग्रहों की खोज"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Improved remote education in rural areas</b><br>ISRO's communication satellites support <b><u>tele-education in rural areas</u></b> – a direct social benefit. Black holes, deep space and exoplanets are scientific research areas.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>SITE (1975–76)</b> – Satellite Instructional Television Experiment, using NASA's ATS-6, took TV education to about 2,400 villages.<br>• <b>EDUSAT (GSAT-3)</b>, launched in <b>2004</b>, was India's first satellite dedicated to education.<br>• Other social uses: <b>telemedicine, disaster warning, Village Resource Centres</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों में बेहतर दूरस्थ शिक्षा</b><br>ISRO के संचार उपग्रह <b><u>ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों में दूरस्थ शिक्षा (Tele-education)</u></b> में सहायता करते हैं – यह प्रत्यक्ष सामाजिक लाभ है। ब्लैक होल, गहन अंतरिक्ष और बाह्यग्रह वैज्ञानिक अनुसंधान के क्षेत्र हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>SITE (1975–76)</b> – उपग्रह शिक्षण टेलीविज़न प्रयोग, NASA के ATS-6 द्वारा लगभग 2,400 गाँवों तक टीवी शिक्षा पहुँचाई।<br>• <b>2004</b> में प्रक्षेपित <b>EDUSAT (GSAT-3)</b> भारत का पहला शिक्षा-समर्पित उपग्रह था।<br>• अन्य सामाजिक उपयोग: <b>टेलीमेडिसिन, आपदा चेतावनी, ग्राम संसाधन केंद्र</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000074411","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Vijayanagara and Bahmani Kingdom","question":{"en":"The Bijapur Sultan who patronized Ibrahim Rauza and Gol Gumbaz was: [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"इब्राहिम रौज़ा और गोल गुंबज़ को संरक्षण देने वाला बीजापुर का सुल्तान कौन था? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Yusuf Adil Shah","hi":"यूसुफ़ आदिल शाह"},"2":{"en":"Ibrahim Adil Shah I","hi":"इब्राहिम आदिल शाह प्रथम"},"3":{"en":"Ibrahim Adil Shah II","hi":"इब्राहिम आदिल शाह द्वितीय"},"4":{"en":"Ali Adil Shah","hi":"अली आदिल शाह"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Ibrahim Adil Shah II</b><br><b><u>Ibrahim Adil Shah II</u></b> (1580–1627) built the <b>Ibrahim Rauza</b> and was the great patron of art and architecture in Bijapur; Adil Shahi architecture reached its peak under him and his successor.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Gol Gumbaz</b> is the tomb of <b>Muhammad Adil Shah</b> (son of Ibrahim II); its dome is among the largest in the world and has a famous <b>\"Whispering Gallery\"</b>.<br>• Ibrahim Adil Shah II wrote <b>Kitab-i-Nauras</b> and was called <b>\"Jagadguru\"</b>.<br>• The Adil Shahi dynasty was founded by <b>Yusuf Adil Shah</b> in <b>1489</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – इब्राहिम आदिल शाह द्वितीय</b><br><b><u>इब्राहिम आदिल शाह द्वितीय</u></b> (1580–1627) ने <b>इब्राहिम रौज़ा</b> बनवाया और वे बीजापुर में कला और स्थापत्य के महान संरक्षक थे; उनके और उनके उत्तराधिकारी के समय आदिलशाही स्थापत्य चरम पर पहुँचा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>गोल गुंबज़</b> <b>मुहम्मद आदिल शाह</b> (इब्राहिम द्वितीय के पुत्र) का मकबरा है; इसका गुंबद विश्व के सबसे बड़े गुंबदों में है और इसमें प्रसिद्ध <b>\"फुसफुसाती गैलरी (Whispering Gallery)\"</b> है।<br>• इब्राहिम आदिल शाह द्वितीय ने <b>किताब-ए-नौरस</b> लिखी और उन्हें <b>\"जगद्गुरु\"</b> कहा गया।<br>• आदिलशाही वंश की स्थापना <b>यूसुफ़ आदिल शाह</b> ने <b>1489</b> में की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000074412","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"Which BRICS (Brazil, Russia, India, China, and South Africa) member is the largest producer of tea? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कौन-सा ब्रिक्स (ब्राज़ील, रूस, भारत, चीन और दक्षिण अफ्रीका) सदस्य चाय का सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"China","hi":"चीन"},"2":{"en":"India","hi":"भारत"},"3":{"en":"Brazil","hi":"ब्राज़ील"},"4":{"en":"South Africa","hi":"दक्षिण अफ्रीका"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – China</b><br><b><u>China</u></b> is the world's largest producer of tea, followed by <b>India</b> in second place.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In India, <b>Assam</b> is the largest tea-producing state, followed by West Bengal.<br>• India is the world's <b>largest consumer</b> of black tea; Tea Board of India HQ: <b>Kolkata</b>.<br>• Tea needs warm humid climate, <b>well-drained slopes</b> and 150–300 cm rainfall.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – चीन</b><br><b><u>चीन</u></b> विश्व का सबसे बड़ा चाय उत्पादक है, जबकि <b>भारत</b> दूसरे स्थान पर है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत में <b>असम</b> सबसे बड़ा चाय उत्पादक राज्य है, उसके बाद पश्चिम बंगाल।<br>• भारत काली चाय का विश्व का <b>सबसे बड़ा उपभोक्ता</b> है; भारतीय चाय बोर्ड का मुख्यालय: <b>कोलकाता</b>।<br>• चाय के लिए गर्म-आर्द्र जलवायु, <b>अच्छे जल-निकास वाले ढलान</b> और 150–300 cm वर्षा चाहिए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000074413","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"By which of the following buildings is the Gothic Revival architecture introduced during British rule in India best represented ? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"ब्रिटिश शासन के दौरान भारत में शुरू की गई गॉथिक रिवाइवल वास्तुकला का सबसे अच्छा प्रतिनिधित्व निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी इमारत करती है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rashtrapati Bhavan, New Delhi","hi":"राष्ट्रपति भवन, नई दिल्ली"},"2":{"en":"Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Terminus (formerly Victoria Terminus), Mumbai","hi":"छत्रपति शिवाजी महाराज टर्मिनस (पूर्व में विक्टोरिया टर्मिनस), मुंबई"},"3":{"en":"Gateway of India, Mumbai","hi":"गेटवे ऑफ इंडिया, मुंबई"},"4":{"en":"Victoria Memorial, Kolkata","hi":"विक्टोरिया मेमोरियल, कोलकाता"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Terminus (formerly Victoria Terminus), Mumbai</b><br><b><u>Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Terminus</u></b>, designed by <b>F.W. Stevens</b> and completed in <b>1888</b>, is the finest example of <b>Victorian Gothic Revival</b> architecture blended with Indian elements.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• CSMT was declared a <b>UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2004</b>.<br>• <b>Gateway of India</b> – Indo-Saracenic style; <b>Victoria Memorial</b> – Indo-Saracenic with white Makrana marble.<br>• <b>Rashtrapati Bhavan</b> was designed by <b>Edwin Lutyens</b> (Neo-classical blended with Indian features).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – छत्रपति शिवाजी महाराज टर्मिनस (पूर्व में विक्टोरिया टर्मिनस), मुंबई</b><br><b>एफ.डब्ल्यू. स्टीवंस</b> द्वारा डिज़ाइन और <b>1888</b> में पूर्ण <b><u>छत्रपति शिवाजी महाराज टर्मिनस</u></b> भारतीय तत्वों के साथ <b>विक्टोरियन गॉथिक रिवाइवल</b> वास्तुकला का सर्वोत्तम उदाहरण है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• CSMT को <b>2004 में यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल</b> घोषित किया गया।<br>• <b>गेटवे ऑफ इंडिया</b> – इंडो-सारसेनिक शैली; <b>विक्टोरिया मेमोरियल</b> – सफ़ेद मकराना संगमरमर से बनी इंडो-सारसेनिक शैली।<br>• <b>राष्ट्रपति भवन</b> को <b>एडविन लुटियंस</b> ने डिज़ाइन किया (भारतीय विशेषताओं के साथ नव-शास्त्रीय शैली)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000074414","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Awards and Honours","question":{"en":"Who among the following was NOT awarded the Nobel Prize for Literature? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किसे साहित्य का नोबेल पुरस्कार नहीं मिला? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rabindranath Tagore","hi":"रवींद्रनाथ टैगोर"},"2":{"en":"V.S. Naipaul","hi":"वी.एस. नायपॉल"},"3":{"en":"R.K. Narayan","hi":"आर.के. नारायण"},"4":{"en":"Kazuo Ishiguro","hi":"काज़ुओ इशिगुरो"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – R.K. Narayan</b><br><b><u>R.K. Narayan</u></b> never won the Nobel Prize, although he was a celebrated novelist. Tagore (1913), V.S. Naipaul (2001) and Kazuo Ishiguro (2017) are Nobel laureates in Literature.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Tagore</b> was the first Asian Nobel laureate, for <b>Gitanjali</b>.<br>• R.K. Narayan created the fictional town <b>Malgudi</b>; he won the <b>Sahitya Akademi Award</b> for <b>The Guide</b> (1960).<br>• Nobel Prize in Literature <b>2024</b>: <b>Han Kang</b> (South Korea); <b>2025</b>: <b>László Krasznahorkai</b> (Hungary).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – आर.के. नारायण</b><br><b><u>आर.के. नारायण</u></b> को प्रसिद्ध उपन्यासकार होने के बावजूद नोबेल पुरस्कार नहीं मिला। टैगोर (1913), वी.एस. नायपॉल (2001) और काज़ुओ इशिगुरो (2017) साहित्य के नोबेल विजेता हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>टैगोर</b> <b>गीतांजलि</b> के लिए नोबेल पाने वाले पहले एशियाई थे।<br>• आर.के. नारायण ने काल्पनिक नगर <b>मालगुडी</b> रचा; उन्हें <b>द गाइड</b> के लिए <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार</b> (1960) मिला।<br>• साहित्य का नोबेल <b>2024</b>: <b>हान कांग</b> (दक्षिण कोरिया); <b>2025</b>: <b>लास्लो क्रास्नाहोरकाई</b> (हंगरी)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000074415","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Banking","question":{"en":"Which of the following Indian institutions established during the 6<sup>th</sup> Five-Year Plan was tasked with strengthening external trade financing? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"छठी पंचवर्षीय योजना के दौरान स्थापित निम्नलिखित में से किस भारतीय संस्था को बाह्य व्यापार वित्तपोषण को सुदृढ़ करने का कार्य सौंपा गया? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"State Bank of India (SBI)","hi":"भारतीय स्टेट बैंक (SBI)"},"2":{"en":"Small Industries Development Bank of India (SIDBI)","hi":"भारतीय लघु उद्योग विकास बैंक (SIDBI)"},"3":{"en":"Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India (IRDA )","hi":"भारतीय बीमा विनियामक और विकास प्राधिकरण (IRDA )"},"4":{"en":"The Export-Import Bank of India (EXIM Bank)","hi":"भारतीय निर्यात-आयात बैंक (EXIM बैंक)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – The Export-Import Bank of India (EXIM Bank)</b><br>The <b><u>EXIM Bank</u></b> was set up on <b>1 January 1982</b> (Sixth Plan, 1980–85) under the EXIM Bank Act, 1981 to <b>finance, facilitate and promote India's foreign trade</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• EXIM Bank HQ: <b>Mumbai</b>; wholly owned by the Government of India.<br>• <b>NABARD</b> was also set up in 1982 (Sixth Plan).<br>• <b>SIDBI</b> – 1990; <b>SBI</b> – 1955 (from Imperial Bank); <b>IRDA</b> – 1999.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – भारतीय निर्यात-आयात बैंक (EXIM बैंक)</b><br><b><u>EXIM बैंक</u></b> की स्थापना EXIM बैंक अधिनियम, 1981 के तहत <b>1 जनवरी 1982</b> (छठी योजना, 1980–85) को <b>भारत के विदेशी व्यापार के वित्तपोषण, सुविधा और संवर्धन</b> के लिए की गई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• EXIM बैंक मुख्यालय: <b>मुंबई</b>; पूर्णतः भारत सरकार के स्वामित्व में।<br>• <b>नाबार्ड (NABARD)</b> भी 1982 (छठी योजना) में स्थापित हुआ।<br>• <b>SIDBI</b> – 1990; <b>SBI</b> – 1955 (इंपीरियल बैंक से); <b>IRDA</b> – 1999।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000074416","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Awards and Honours","question":{"en":"Which Polish author was awarded the Nobel Prize in Literature in 2018 for her narrative imagination? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किस पोलिश लेखिका को उनकी कथात्मक कल्पना के लिए 2018 में साहित्य का नोबेल पुरस्कार दिया गया? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Wisława Szymborska","hi":"विस्वावा शिम्बोर्स्का"},"2":{"en":"Olga Tokarczuk","hi":"ओल्गा तोकार्चुक"},"3":{"en":"Dorota Masłowska","hi":"दोरोता मास्लोव्स्का"},"4":{"en":"Hanna Krall","hi":"हन्ना क्राल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Olga Tokarczuk</b><br><b><u>Olga Tokarczuk</u></b> received the <b>2018 Nobel Prize in Literature</b> (announced in 2019) \"for a narrative imagination that with encyclopedic passion represents the crossing of boundaries as a form of life\".<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 2018 prize was announced in <b>2019</b> along with the 2019 prize to <b>Peter Handke</b>, because of a scandal at the Swedish Academy.<br>• Tokarczuk also won the <b>Man Booker International Prize 2018</b> for <b>Flights</b>.<br>• <b>Wisława Szymborska</b>, another Polish writer, won the Nobel in <b>1996</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ओल्गा तोकार्चुक</b><br><b><u>ओल्गा तोकार्चुक</u></b> को <b>2018 का साहित्य नोबेल पुरस्कार</b> (2019 में घोषित) \"विश्वकोशीय उत्साह के साथ सीमाओं के पार जाने को जीवन के रूप में प्रस्तुत करने वाली कथात्मक कल्पना\" के लिए मिला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• स्वीडिश अकादमी में विवाद के कारण 2018 का पुरस्कार <b>2019</b> में <b>पीटर हैंडके</b> के 2019 पुरस्कार के साथ घोषित हुआ।<br>• तोकार्चुक ने <b>फ्लाइट्स</b> के लिए <b>मैन बुकर इंटरनेशनल पुरस्कार 2018</b> भी जीता।<br>• एक अन्य पोलिश लेखिका <b>विस्वावा शिम्बोर्स्का</b> ने <b>1996</b> में नोबेल जीता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000074417","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"At the confluence of which two water bodies do thousands of pilgrims gather to take a holy dip during the Ganga Sagar Mela? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"गंगासागर मेले के दौरान हज़ारों तीर्थयात्री किन दो जल निकायों के संगम पर पवित्र डुबकी लगाने के लिए एकत्र होते हैं? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ganga and the Bay of Bengal","hi":"गंगा और बंगाल की खाड़ी"},"2":{"en":"Yamuna and Arabian Sea","hi":"यमुना और अरब सागर"},"3":{"en":"Brahmaputra and Bay of Bengal","hi":"ब्रह्मपुत्र और बंगाल की खाड़ी"},"4":{"en":"Narmada and Indian Ocean","hi":"नर्मदा और हिंद महासागर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Ganga and the Bay of Bengal</b><br>The <b>Ganga Sagar Mela</b> is held on <b>Sagar Island</b> (West Bengal) on <b>Makar Sankranti</b>, where pilgrims bathe at the confluence of the <b><u>Ganga (Hooghly) and the Bay of Bengal</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Kapil Muni Temple</b> on Sagar Island is the centre of the mela.<br>• It is considered the <b>second-largest congregation</b> of Hindus after the Kumbh Mela.<br>• Sagar Island lies in the <b>South 24 Parganas</b> district, near the Sundarbans.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – गंगा और बंगाल की खाड़ी</b><br><b>गंगासागर मेला</b> <b>मकर संक्रांति</b> पर <b>सागर द्वीप</b> (पश्चिम बंगाल) में लगता है, जहाँ तीर्थयात्री <b><u>गंगा (हुगली) और बंगाल की खाड़ी</u></b> के संगम पर स्नान करते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सागर द्वीप पर <b>कपिल मुनि मंदिर</b> मेले का केंद्र है।<br>• इसे कुंभ मेले के बाद हिंदुओं का <b>दूसरा सबसे बड़ा समागम</b> माना जाता है।<br>• सागर द्वीप सुंदरबन के निकट <b>दक्षिण 24 परगना</b> ज़िले में है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000074418","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The \"Wood's Despatch\" of 1854 is considered a landmark in the history of Indian education because it: [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1854 का \"वुड का डिस्पैच\" भारतीय शिक्षा के इतिहास में एक मील का पत्थर माना जाता है क्योंकि इसने: [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Advocated for the complete withdrawal of government support from education.","hi":"शिक्षा से सरकारी सहायता पूरी तरह वापस लेने की वकालत की।"},"2":{"en":"Proposed the establishment of universities in the presidency towns of Calcutta, Bombay, and Madras.","hi":"कलकत्ता, बंबई और मद्रास के प्रेसीडेंसी नगरों में विश्वविद्यालयों की स्थापना का प्रस्ताव रखा।"},"3":{"en":"Recommended that Sanskrit and Persian should be the primary languages of instruction.","hi":"संस्कृत और फ़ारसी को शिक्षा की प्राथमिक भाषा बनाने की सिफारिश की।"},"4":{"en":"Led to the immediate implementation of free and compulsory primary education across India.","hi":"पूरे भारत में तुरंत निःशुल्क और अनिवार्य प्राथमिक शिक्षा लागू कराई।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Proposed the establishment of universities in the presidency towns of Calcutta, Bombay, and Madras.</b><br><b>Wood's Despatch (1854)</b>, sent by <b>Charles Wood</b>, proposed <b><u>universities in Calcutta, Bombay and Madras</u></b> on the model of London University; these were set up in <b>1857</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It is called the <b>\"Magna Carta of English Education in India\"</b>.<br>• It recommended a graded system – <b>primary schools, high schools, colleges, universities</b> – and grants-in-aid.<br>• It proposed English for higher education and <b>vernaculars at the school level</b>; it was issued during <b>Lord Dalhousie's</b> time.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कलकत्ता, बंबई और मद्रास के प्रेसीडेंसी नगरों में विश्वविद्यालयों की स्थापना का प्रस्ताव रखा।</b><br><b>चार्ल्स वुड</b> द्वारा भेजे गए <b>वुड के डिस्पैच (1854)</b> ने लंदन विश्वविद्यालय के मॉडल पर <b><u>कलकत्ता, बंबई और मद्रास में विश्वविद्यालयों</u></b> का प्रस्ताव रखा; ये <b>1857</b> में स्थापित हुए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसे <b>\"भारत में अंग्रेज़ी शिक्षा का मैग्नाकार्टा\"</b> कहा जाता है।<br>• इसने श्रेणीबद्ध व्यवस्था – <b>प्राथमिक विद्यालय, हाई स्कूल, कॉलेज, विश्वविद्यालय</b> – और अनुदान सहायता की सिफारिश की।<br>• इसने उच्च शिक्षा के लिए अंग्रेज़ी और <b>विद्यालय स्तर पर देशी भाषाओं</b> का प्रस्ताव रखा; यह <b>लॉर्ड डलहौज़ी</b> के समय जारी हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000074419","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: State News","question":{"en":"Which is the first state in the country to have its own Internet Service Provider (ISP) license from the Department of Telecommunications? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दूरसंचार विभाग से अपना स्वयं का इंटरनेट सेवा प्रदाता (ISP) लाइसेंस पाने वाला देश का पहला राज्य कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Kerala","hi":"केरल"},"2":{"en":"Andhra Pradesh","hi":"आंध्र प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"Delhi","hi":"दिल्ली"},"4":{"en":"Punjab","hi":"पंजाब"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Kerala</b><br><b><u>Kerala</u></b> became the first state to get its own ISP licence (2022) through <b>KFON – Kerala Fibre Optic Network</b>, which aims to provide affordable internet to all households.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• KFON aims to provide <b>free internet to BPL families</b>.<br>• Kerala declared <b>internet access a basic right</b> in 2017.<br>• Kerala was declared India's first <b>fully digitally literate state</b> in 2025.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केरल</b><br><b><u>केरल</u></b> <b>KFON – केरल फाइबर ऑप्टिक नेटवर्क</b> के माध्यम से अपना स्वयं का ISP लाइसेंस (2022) पाने वाला पहला राज्य बना, जिसका लक्ष्य सभी परिवारों को सस्ता इंटरनेट देना है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• KFON का लक्ष्य <b>BPL परिवारों को मुफ्त इंटरनेट</b> देना है।<br>• केरल ने 2017 में <b>इंटरनेट पहुँच को मूल अधिकार</b> घोषित किया।<br>• केरल को 2025 में भारत का पहला <b>पूर्ण डिजिटल साक्षर राज्य</b> घोषित किया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000074420","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"With 18 Grand Slam titles, who among the following is considered India's most successful tennis players? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"18 ग्रैंड स्लैम खिताबों के साथ, निम्नलिखित में से किसे भारत का सबसे सफल टेनिस खिलाड़ी माना जाता है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rohan Bopanna","hi":"रोहन बोपन्ना"},"2":{"en":"Sania Mirza","hi":"सानिया मिर्ज़ा"},"3":{"en":"Mahesh Bhupati","hi":"महेश भूपति"},"4":{"en":"Leander Paes","hi":"लिएंडर पेस"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Leander Paes</b><br><b><u>Leander Paes</u></b> has won <b>18 Grand Slam titles</b> – <b>8 men's doubles and 10 mixed doubles</b> – making him India's most successful tennis player.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Paes won the <b>bronze medal</b> at the <b>1996 Atlanta Olympics</b> (singles).<br>• He completed a <b>career Grand Slam</b> in both men's doubles and mixed doubles.<br>• He played in a record <b>7 Olympic Games</b> (1992–2016); inducted into the International Tennis Hall of Fame in 2024.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – लिएंडर पेस</b><br><b><u>लिएंडर पेस</u></b> ने <b>18 ग्रैंड स्लैम खिताब</b> – <b>8 पुरुष युगल और 10 मिश्रित युगल</b> – जीते हैं, जिससे वे भारत के सबसे सफल टेनिस खिलाड़ी हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पेस ने <b>1996 अटलांटा ओलंपिक</b> (एकल) में <b>कांस्य पदक</b> जीता।<br>• उन्होंने पुरुष युगल और मिश्रित युगल दोनों में <b>करियर ग्रैंड स्लैम</b> पूरा किया।<br>• उन्होंने रिकॉर्ड <b>7 ओलंपिक खेलों</b> (1992–2016) में भाग लिया; 2024 में अंतर्राष्ट्रीय टेनिस हॉल ऑफ फेम में शामिल।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000074421","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Natural gas reserves of India occur in which of the following regions? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत के प्राकृतिक गैस भंडार निम्नलिखित में से किस क्षेत्र में पाए जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The western offshore region near Maharashtra","hi":"महाराष्ट्र के निकट पश्चिमी अपतटीय क्षेत्र"},"2":{"en":"The coalfields of Jharkhand and West Bengal","hi":"झारखंड और पश्चिम बंगाल के कोयला क्षेत्र"},"3":{"en":"The Deccan Plateau in Karnataka","hi":"कर्नाटक का दक्कन पठार"},"4":{"en":"The Himalayan foothills in Uttarakhand","hi":"उत्तराखंड की हिमालयी तलहटी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – The western offshore region near Maharashtra</b><br>India's major natural gas reserves are found with petroleum in the <b><u>western offshore region near Maharashtra</u></b> (Mumbai High and Bassein), as well as in the Krishna-Godavari basin and Gujarat.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Krishna-Godavari (KG) basin</b> has large gas finds on the east coast.<br>• The <b>Hazira–Vijaipur–Jagdishpur (HVJ) pipeline</b> carries gas from Mumbai High to the north.<br>• <b>GAIL</b> is India's largest natural gas transmission company; CNG is used as a cleaner fuel.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – महाराष्ट्र के निकट पश्चिमी अपतटीय क्षेत्र</b><br>भारत के प्रमुख प्राकृतिक गैस भंडार पेट्रोलियम के साथ <b><u>महाराष्ट्र के निकट पश्चिमी अपतटीय क्षेत्र</u></b> (मुंबई हाई और बसीन) तथा कृष्णा-गोदावरी बेसिन और गुजरात में पाए जाते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पूर्वी तट पर <b>कृष्णा-गोदावरी (KG) बेसिन</b> में बड़े गैस भंडार मिले हैं।<br>• <b>हजीरा–विजयपुर–जगदीशपुर (HVJ) पाइपलाइन</b> मुंबई हाई से गैस उत्तर तक ले जाती है।<br>• <b>GAIL</b> भारत की सबसे बड़ी प्राकृतिक गैस पारेषण कंपनी है; CNG स्वच्छ ईंधन के रूप में उपयोग होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000074422","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which of the following is not included in the women’s heptathlon? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी स्पर्धा महिलाओं के हेप्टाथलॉन में शामिल नहीं है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"100 metres hurdles","hi":"100 मीटर बाधा दौड़"},"2":{"en":"Javelin throw","hi":"भाला फेंक"},"3":{"en":"400 metres","hi":"400 मीटर"},"4":{"en":"Shot put","hi":"गोला फेंक"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 400 metres</b><br>The women's heptathlon has seven events: <b>100 m hurdles, high jump, shot put, 200 m</b> (day 1) and <b>long jump, javelin throw, 800 m</b> (day 2). <b><u>400 m</u></b> is not part of it.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 400 m is part of the men's <b>decathlon</b> (10 events).<br>• <b>Swapna Barman</b> won India's first heptathlon gold at the <b>2018 Asian Games</b>.<br>• Heptathlon world record holder: <b>Jackie Joyner-Kersee</b> (7,291 points).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 400 मीटर</b><br>महिलाओं के हेप्टाथलॉन में सात स्पर्धाएँ हैं: <b>100 मीटर बाधा दौड़, ऊँची कूद, गोला फेंक, 200 मीटर</b> (पहला दिन) तथा <b>लंबी कूद, भाला फेंक, 800 मीटर</b> (दूसरा दिन)। <b><u>400 मीटर</u></b> इसमें शामिल नहीं है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 400 मीटर पुरुषों के <b>डेकाथलॉन</b> (10 स्पर्धाएँ) का भाग है।<br>• <b>स्वप्ना बर्मन</b> ने <b>2018 एशियाई खेलों</b> में भारत का पहला हेप्टाथलॉन स्वर्ण जीता।<br>• हेप्टाथलॉन विश्व रिकॉर्डधारी: <b>जैकी जॉयनर-केर्सी</b> (7,291 अंक)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000074423","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"<b>Consider the following statements about the Beach Games 2024 held in Diu:</b><br>1) Madhya Pradesh topped the medal tally with 18 medals, including 7 golds.<br>2) Maharashtra won the gold medal in Beach Soccer by defeating Lakshadweep in the final.<br><b>Which of the statements is/are correct?</b> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"<b>दीव में आयोजित बीच गेम्स 2024 के बारे में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:</b><br>1) मध्य प्रदेश 7 स्वर्ण सहित 18 पदकों के साथ पदक तालिका में शीर्ष पर रहा।<br>2) महाराष्ट्र ने फाइनल में लक्षद्वीप को हराकर बीच सॉकर में स्वर्ण पदक जीता।<br><b>कौन-सा/से कथन सही है/हैं?</b> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1 is Correct","hi":"केवल 1 सही है"},"2":{"en":"Only 2 is Correct","hi":"केवल 2 सही है"},"3":{"en":"1 and 2 are Correct","hi":"1 और 2 सही हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2 is Correct","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2 सही है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Only 1 is Correct</b><br>At the <b>first-ever Beach Games (Diu, January 2024)</b>, landlocked <b>Madhya Pradesh</b> emerged overall champion with <b>18 medals including 7 golds</b>, so statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 about the beach soccer final is not correct. Hence <b><u>Only 1</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The games were held from <b>4 to 11 January 2024</b> at <b>Ghoghla Beach, Diu</b>, under <b>Khelo India</b>.<br>• Sports included <b>beach soccer, beach volleyball, beach kabaddi, sepak takraw, pencak silat, mallakhamb, sea swimming and tug of war</b>.<br>• Diu is part of the UT of <b>Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केवल 1 सही है</b><br><b>पहले बीच गेम्स (दीव, जनवरी 2024)</b> में स्थलरुद्ध <b>मध्य प्रदेश</b> <b>7 स्वर्ण सहित 18 पदकों</b> के साथ समग्र चैंपियन बना, अतः कथन 1 सही है। बीच सॉकर फाइनल के बारे में कथन 2 सही नहीं है। अतः <b><u>केवल 1</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ये खेल <b>खेलो इंडिया</b> के तहत <b>4 से 11 जनवरी 2024</b> तक <b>घोघला बीच, दीव</b> में हुए।<br>• खेलों में <b>बीच सॉकर, बीच वॉलीबॉल, बीच कबड्डी, सेपक टकरा, पेनकक सिलाट, मल्लखंभ, समुद्री तैराकी और रस्साकशी</b> शामिल थे।<br>• दीव केंद्रशासित प्रदेश <b>दादरा और नगर हवेली तथा दमन और दीव</b> का भाग है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000074424","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Salient Features of the Constitution","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements:<br>1. India is a federal state as it has a written constitution.<br>2. The term 'quasi-federal' was used by K.C. Wheare to describe India's federalism.<br>Which of the statements is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1. भारत एक संघीय राज्य है क्योंकि इसका संविधान लिखित है।<br>2. 'अर्ध-संघीय' शब्द का प्रयोग के.सी. व्हेयर ने भारत के संघवाद का वर्णन करने के लिए किया।<br>कौन-सा/से कथन <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"Only 2","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Only 2</b><br>A written constitution alone does not make a state federal (unitary states can also have written constitutions), so statement 1 is wrong. <b>K.C. Wheare</b> described the Indian Constitution as <b>\"quasi-federal\"</b>, so statement 2 is correct: <b><u>Only 2</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The word <b>\"federation\"</b> is not used in the Constitution; Article 1 calls India a <b>\"Union of States\"</b>.<br>• <b>Granville Austin</b> called it <b>\"cooperative federalism\"</b>; <b>Ivor Jennings</b> – \"federation with a strong centralising tendency\".<br>• Federal features: dual polity, division of powers, rigid constitution, independent judiciary, bicameralism.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – केवल 2</b><br>केवल लिखित संविधान से कोई राज्य संघीय नहीं बनता (एकात्मक राज्यों के भी लिखित संविधान हो सकते हैं), अतः कथन 1 गलत है। <b>के.सी. व्हेयर</b> ने भारतीय संविधान को <b>\"अर्ध-संघीय (Quasi-federal)\"</b> कहा, अतः कथन 2 सही है: <b><u>केवल 2</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• संविधान में <b>\"संघ (Federation)\"</b> शब्द का प्रयोग नहीं है; अनुच्छेद 1 भारत को <b>\"राज्यों का संघ\"</b> कहता है।<br>• <b>ग्रैनविल ऑस्टिन</b> ने इसे <b>\"सहकारी संघवाद\"</b> कहा; <b>आइवर जेनिंग्स</b> – \"सशक्त केंद्रीकरण प्रवृत्ति वाला संघ\"।<br>• संघीय विशेषताएँ: द्वैध शासन, शक्तियों का विभाजन, कठोर संविधान, स्वतंत्र न्यायपालिका, द्विसदनीयता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000074425","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Local Government","question":{"en":"Which Schedule of the Indian Constitution contains provisions related to the Panchayati Raj system? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान की किस अनुसूची में पंचायती राज व्यवस्था से संबंधित प्रावधान हैं? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9<sup>th</sup> Schedule","hi":"9वीं अनुसूची"},"2":{"en":"10<sup>th</sup> Schedule","hi":"10वीं अनुसूची"},"3":{"en":"11<sup>th</sup> Schedule","hi":"11वीं अनुसूची"},"4":{"en":"12<sup>th</sup> Schedule","hi":"12वीं अनुसूची"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 11<sup>th</sup> Schedule</b><br>The <b><u>11<sup>th</sup> Schedule</u></b>, added by the <b>73<sup>rd</sup> Amendment Act, 1992</b>, lists <b>29 subjects</b> under the functional domain of Panchayats (Article 243G).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>12<sup>th</sup> Schedule</b> – Municipalities, 18 subjects (74<sup>th</sup> Amendment).<br>• <b>10<sup>th</sup> Schedule</b> – Anti-defection law (52<sup>nd</sup> Amendment, 1985).<br>• <b>9<sup>th</sup> Schedule</b> – added by the 1<sup>st</sup> Amendment (1951) to protect land reform laws.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 11वीं अनुसूची</b><br><b>73वें संशोधन अधिनियम, 1992</b> द्वारा जोड़ी गई <b><u>11वीं अनुसूची</u></b> में पंचायतों के कार्यक्षेत्र (अनुच्छेद 243G) के <b>29 विषय</b> हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>12वीं अनुसूची</b> – नगरपालिकाएँ, 18 विषय (74वाँ संशोधन)।<br>• <b>10वीं अनुसूची</b> – दल-बदल विरोधी कानून (52वाँ संशोधन, 1985)।<br>• <b>9वीं अनुसूची</b> – भूमि सुधार कानूनों की रक्षा हेतु पहले संशोधन (1951) द्वारा जोड़ी गई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000074426","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"According to the theory of continental drift, what was the name of the single large landmass that originally existed on Earth? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"महाद्वीपीय विस्थापन सिद्धांत के अनुसार पृथ्वी पर मूल रूप से विद्यमान एकल विशाल भूभाग का नाम क्या था? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Panthalassa","hi":"पैंथालासा"},"2":{"en":"Pangaea","hi":"पैंजिया"},"3":{"en":"Gondwanaland","hi":"गोंडवानालैंड"},"4":{"en":"Laurasia","hi":"लॉरेशिया"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Pangaea</b><br>According to <b>Alfred Wegener's Continental Drift Theory (1912)</b>, all continents were once joined in a single supercontinent called <b><u>Pangaea</u></b>, surrounded by one mega-ocean.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The mega-ocean around Pangaea was <b>Panthalassa</b>.<br>• Pangaea split into <b>Laurasia</b> (north) and <b>Gondwanaland</b> (south), separated by the <b>Tethys Sea</b>.<br>• Evidence: <b>jig-saw fit</b> of continents, similar rocks and fossils (e.g., <b>Mesosaurus</b>), tillite deposits.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पैंजिया</b><br><b>अल्फ्रेड वेगनर के महाद्वीपीय विस्थापन सिद्धांत (1912)</b> के अनुसार सभी महाद्वीप एक समय <b><u>पैंजिया (Pangaea)</u></b> नामक एक विशाल महाद्वीप के रूप में जुड़े थे, जो एक महासागर से घिरा था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पैंजिया के चारों ओर का विशाल महासागर <b>पैंथालासा</b> था।<br>• पैंजिया <b>लॉरेशिया</b> (उत्तर) और <b>गोंडवानालैंड</b> (दक्षिण) में टूटा, जिनके बीच <b>टेथिस सागर</b> था।<br>• प्रमाण: महाद्वीपों का <b>साम्य (Jig-saw fit)</b>, समान चट्टानें और जीवाश्म (जैसे <b>मेसोसॉरस</b>), टिलाइट निक्षेप।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000074427","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Atmosphere","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements about the exosphere:<br>1. Gas particles in this layer are so less in numbers that collisions between them are extremely rare.<br>2. This layer has high air density and significant weather activity.<br>Which of the statements given is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"बहिर्मंडल के बारे में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1. इस परत में गैस कण इतने कम हैं कि उनके बीच टक्कर अत्यंत दुर्लभ होती है।<br>2. इस परत में वायु घनत्व अधिक है और मौसमी गतिविधियाँ महत्वपूर्ण हैं।<br>दिए गए कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"Only 2","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2 are correct","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों सही हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2 is correct","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2 सही है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Only 1</b><br>The <b>exosphere</b> is the outermost layer, where air is extremely thin and particles rarely collide (statement 1 correct). Weather occurs in the <b>troposphere</b>, not the exosphere (statement 2 wrong). Hence <b><u>Only 1</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Layers from bottom: <b>Troposphere → Stratosphere → Mesosphere → Thermosphere → Exosphere</b>.<br>• Light gases like <b>hydrogen and helium</b> escape into space from the exosphere.<br>• Most <b>satellites</b> orbit in the thermosphere and exosphere.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केवल 1</b><br><b>बहिर्मंडल (Exosphere)</b> सबसे बाहरी परत है, जहाँ वायु अत्यंत विरल है और कण शायद ही टकराते हैं (कथन 1 सही)। मौसमी घटनाएँ <b>क्षोभमंडल (Troposphere)</b> में होती हैं, बहिर्मंडल में नहीं (कथन 2 गलत)। अतः <b><u>केवल 1</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• नीचे से परतें: <b>क्षोभमंडल → समतापमंडल → मध्यमंडल → तापमंडल → बहिर्मंडल</b>।<br>• <b>हाइड्रोजन और हीलियम</b> जैसी हल्की गैसें बहिर्मंडल से अंतरिक्ष में निकल जाती हैं।<br>• अधिकांश <b>उपग्रह</b> तापमंडल और बहिर्मंडल में परिक्रमा करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000074428","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which development during the post-1991 reform period enabled services such as accounting, banking, music recording, film editing and clinical advice to be outsourced to India? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1991 के बाद के सुधार काल में किस विकास ने लेखांकन, बैंकिंग, संगीत रिकॉर्डिंग, फ़िल्म संपादन और नैदानिक परामर्श जैसी सेवाओं को भारत में आउटसोर्स करना संभव बनाया? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Expansion of digital communication networks","hi":"डिजिटल संचार नेटवर्कों का विस्तार"},"2":{"en":"Liberalisation of foreign trade policies","hi":"विदेशी व्यापार नीतियों का उदारीकरण"},"3":{"en":"Improvement in telecommunication links","hi":"दूरसंचार संपर्कों में सुधार"},"4":{"en":"Growth of public sector enterprises","hi":"सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के उद्यमों की वृद्धि"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Improvement in telecommunication links</b><br>As per NCERT, with the <b><u>improvement in telecommunication links</u></b> and IT, services like accounting, banking, music recording, film editing, book transcription and clinical advice could be outsourced to India and delivered over the internet.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Outsourcing</b> – a company hires regular services from external sources, often from other countries.<br>• India's advantages: <b>low wages, skilled manpower and English proficiency</b>.<br>• Outsourcing is regarded as an outcome of <b>globalisation</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – दूरसंचार संपर्कों में सुधार</b><br>NCERT के अनुसार <b><u>दूरसंचार संपर्कों में सुधार</u></b> और IT के कारण लेखांकन, बैंकिंग, संगीत रिकॉर्डिंग, फ़िल्म संपादन, पुस्तक प्रतिलेखन और नैदानिक परामर्श जैसी सेवाएँ भारत को आउटसोर्स करके इंटरनेट से प्रदान की जा सकीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>आउटसोर्सिंग</b> – कंपनी बाहरी स्रोतों, प्रायः अन्य देशों से नियमित सेवाएँ लेती है।<br>• भारत के लाभ: <b>कम मज़दूरी, कुशल जनशक्ति और अंग्रेज़ी दक्षता</b>।<br>• आउटसोर्सिंग को <b>वैश्वीकरण</b> का परिणाम माना जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000074429","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Electricity","question":{"en":"Two identical point charges separated by a distance (d) exert an electrostatic force (F) on each other. If the distance between them is reduced to \\(\\frac{d}{3}\\), while the charges and the surrounding medium remain unchanged, what will be the new electrostatic force? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दूरी (d) पर स्थित दो समान बिंदु आवेश एक-दूसरे पर स्थिरवैद्युत बल (F) लगाते हैं। यदि आवेशों और आसपास के माध्यम को अपरिवर्तित रखते हुए उनके बीच की दूरी घटाकर \\(\\frac{d}{3}\\) कर दी जाए, तो नया स्थिरवैद्युत बल क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3 (force)","hi":"3 (बल)"},"2":{"en":"6(force)","hi":"6(बल)"},"3":{"en":"9 (force)","hi":"9 (बल)"},"4":{"en":"27 (force)","hi":"27 (बल)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 9 (force)</b><br>By Coulomb's law, \\(F = k\\frac{q_1 q_2}{d^2}\\), so \\(F \\propto \\frac{1}{d^2}\\)<br>\\(F' = \\frac{F}{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^2} = 9F\\)<br>The new force is <b><u>9 times</u></b> the original.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• \\(k = \\frac{1}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0} = 9 \\times 10^9\\) N m² C<sup>−2</sup>.<br>• Like charges repel and unlike charges attract; the force acts along the line joining the charges.<br>• SI unit of charge: <b>coulomb (C)</b>; charge on an electron = \\(1.6 \\times 10^{-19}\\) C.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 9 (बल)</b><br>कूलॉम के नियम से \\(F = k\\frac{q_1 q_2}{d^2}\\), अतः \\(F \\propto \\frac{1}{d^2}\\)<br>\\(F' = \\frac{F}{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^2} = 9F\\)<br>नया बल मूल बल का <b><u>9 गुना</u></b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• \\(k = \\frac{1}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0} = 9 \\times 10^9\\) N m² C<sup>−2</sup>।<br>• सजातीय आवेश प्रतिकर्षित और विजातीय आवेश आकर्षित करते हैं; बल आवेशों को मिलाने वाली रेखा के अनुदिश लगता है।<br>• आवेश का SI मात्रक: <b>कूलॉम (C)</b>; इलेक्ट्रॉन पर आवेश = \\(1.6 \\times 10^{-19}\\) C।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000074430","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Digestion and Respiration","question":{"en":"Which mechanism is primarily responsible for the continuous renewal of the small intestinal epithelium? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"छोटी आंत की उपकला के निरंतर नवीकरण के लिए मुख्य रूप से कौन-सी क्रियाविधि उत्तरदायी है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Uniform division across villi and crypts","hi":"विलाई और क्रिप्ट में एकसमान विभाजन"},"2":{"en":"Stem cell proliferation in crypts producing migrating cells","hi":"क्रिप्ट में स्टेम कोशिकाओं का प्रसार जिससे प्रवासी कोशिकाएँ बनती हैं"},"3":{"en":"Villus tip cells re-entering the cell cycle","hi":"विलस शीर्ष कोशिकाओं का पुनः कोशिका चक्र में प्रवेश"},"4":{"en":"Paneth cells dividing to generate all lineages","hi":"पैनेथ कोशिकाओं का विभाजन कर सभी वंशों को उत्पन्न करना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Stem cell proliferation in crypts producing migrating cells</b><br><b>Stem cells</b> at the base of the <b>crypts of Lieberkühn</b> divide continuously. The new cells <b><u>migrate up the villi</u></b> and are shed at the tips, so the epithelium is renewed every <b>3–5 days</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Villi</b> increase the surface area of the small intestine for absorption.<br>• <b>Paneth cells</b> in the crypts secrete <b>antimicrobial lysozyme</b>; they do not generate all cell types.<br>• The small intestine is the main site of <b>digestion and absorption</b>; its parts are duodenum, jejunum and ileum.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – क्रिप्ट में स्टेम कोशिकाओं का प्रसार जिससे प्रवासी कोशिकाएँ बनती हैं</b><br><b>लिबरकुन की क्रिप्ट (Crypts of Lieberkühn)</b> के आधार पर स्थित <b>स्टेम कोशिकाएँ</b> लगातार विभाजित होती हैं। नई कोशिकाएँ <b><u>विलाई के ऊपर प्रवास</u></b> करती हैं और शीर्ष पर झड़ जाती हैं, जिससे उपकला हर <b>3–5 दिन</b> में नवीकृत होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>विलाई (Villi)</b> अवशोषण के लिए छोटी आंत का सतही क्षेत्रफल बढ़ाते हैं।<br>• क्रिप्ट की <b>पैनेथ कोशिकाएँ</b> <b>रोगाणुरोधी लाइसोज़ाइम</b> स्रावित करती हैं; वे सभी कोशिका प्रकार नहीं बनातीं।<br>• छोटी आंत <b>पाचन और अवशोषण</b> का मुख्य स्थल है; इसके भाग ग्रहणी, मध्यांत्र और शेषांत्र हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000074431","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A sphere has a volume of 512π cm³. By what percentage must its radius be increased for the volume to become 2048π cm³? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक गोले का आयतन 512π cm³ है। आयतन 2048π cm³ होने के लिए उसकी त्रिज्या में कितने प्रतिशत वृद्धि करनी होगी? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"59%"},"2":{"en":"100%"},"3":{"en":"150%"},"4":{"en":"200%"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r_1^3 = 512\\pi \\Rightarrow r_1^3 = 384\\); \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r_2^3 = 2048\\pi \\Rightarrow r_2^3 = 1536\\)<br>\\(\\frac{r_2}{r_1} = \\sqrt[3]{4} = 1.5874\\)<br>Increase \\(= 58.74\\% \\approx \\boxed{59\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 59%.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r_1^3 = 512\\pi \\Rightarrow r_1^3 = 384\\); \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r_2^3 = 2048\\pi \\Rightarrow r_2^3 = 1536\\)<br>\\(\\frac{r_2}{r_1} = \\sqrt[3]{4} = 1.5874\\)<br>वृद्धि \\(= 58.74\\% \\approx \\boxed{59\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 59% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000074432","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A wire of length 132 cm bent into the shape of a circle. Find its radius. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"132 cm लंबे एक तार को वृत्त के आकार में मोड़ा जाता है। उसकी त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"21 cm"},"2":{"en":"18 cm"},"3":{"en":"22 cm"},"4":{"en":"14 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Circumference \\(= 2\\pi r = 132\\)<br>\\(2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times r = 132 \\Rightarrow r = \\frac{132 \\times 7}{44}\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{21\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 21 cm.</b>","hi":"परिधि \\(= 2\\pi r = 132\\)<br>\\(2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times r = 132 \\Rightarrow r = \\frac{132 \\times 7}{44}\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{21\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 21 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000074433","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Simplify: (1 − cos²θ)(1 + tan²θ) [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"सरलीकृत कीजिए: (1 − cos²θ)(1 + tan²θ) [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"cot²θ"},"3":{"en":"sin²θ·sec²θ"},"4":{"en":"sec²θ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(1 - \\cos^2\\theta = \\sin^2\\theta\\) and \\(1 + \\tan^2\\theta = \\sec^2\\theta\\)<br>Product \\(= \\sin^2\\theta \\cdot \\sec^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sin^2\\theta \\sec^2\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): sin²θ·sec²θ.</b>","hi":"\\(1 - \\cos^2\\theta = \\sin^2\\theta\\) और \\(1 + \\tan^2\\theta = \\sec^2\\theta\\)<br>गुणनफल \\(= \\sin^2\\theta \\cdot \\sec^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sin^2\\theta \\sec^2\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): sin²θ·sec²θ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000074434","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The volume of a right circular cone with a height of 27 cm is 81π cm³. What is the diameter of its base? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"27 cm ऊँचाई वाले एक लंब वृत्तीय शंकु का आयतन 81π cm³ है। उसके आधार का व्यास क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 cm"},"2":{"en":"16 cm"},"3":{"en":"7 cm"},"4":{"en":"6 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 (27) = 81\\pi\\)<br>\\(9r^2 = 81 \\Rightarrow r = 3\\) cm<br>Diameter \\(= 2r = \\boxed{6\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 6 cm.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 (27) = 81\\pi\\)<br>\\(9r^2 = 81 \\Rightarrow r = 3\\) cm<br>व्यास \\(= 2r = \\boxed{6\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 6 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000074435","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"Find the volume of a triangular pyramid whose base has sides 5 cm, 5 cm, and 6 cm, and whose height is 8 cm. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उस त्रिभुजाकार पिरामिड का आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए जिसके आधार की भुजाएँ 5 cm, 5 cm और 6 cm हैं तथा ऊँचाई 8 cm है। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"16 cm³"},"2":{"en":"18 cm³"},"3":{"en":"10 cm³"},"4":{"en":"32 cm³"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Base height \\(= \\sqrt{5^2 - 3^2} = 4\\) cm, so base area \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 4 = 12\\) cm²<br>Volume \\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times 12 \\times 8\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{32\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 32 cm³.</b>","hi":"आधार की ऊँचाई \\(= \\sqrt{5^2 - 3^2} = 4\\) cm, अतः आधार क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 4 = 12\\) cm²<br>आयतन \\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times 12 \\times 8\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{32\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 32 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000074436","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"What is the value of \\(\\frac{p^3 - q^3}{p - q} - 3pq\\), if p = 7.85 and q = 2.15? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि p = 7.85 और q = 2.15 है, तो \\(\\frac{p^3 - q^3}{p - q} - 3pq\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18.76"},"2":{"en":"32.49"},"3":{"en":"25.87"},"4":{"en":"49.87"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{p^3 - q^3}{p - q} = p^2 + pq + q^2\\)<br>\\(p^2 + pq + q^2 - 3pq = (p - q)^2\\)<br>\\(= (7.85 - 2.15)^2 = (5.7)^2 = \\boxed{32.49}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 32.49.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{p^3 - q^3}{p - q} = p^2 + pq + q^2\\)<br>\\(p^2 + pq + q^2 - 3pq = (p - q)^2\\)<br>\\(= (7.85 - 2.15)^2 = (5.7)^2 = \\boxed{32.49}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 32.49 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000074437","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"40% of Asha's income is equal to 50% of Neha's income. If Asha's income is reduced by ₹200, while Neha's income remains unchanged, the ratio of their new incomes becomes 3: 4. Find Neha's income. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आशा की आय का 40%, नेहा की आय के 50% के बराबर है। यदि आशा की आय ₹200 कम हो जाए और नेहा की आय अपरिवर्तित रहे, तो उनकी नई आयों का अनुपात 3:4 हो जाता है। नेहा की आय ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹350"},"2":{"en":"₹700"},"3":{"en":"₹630"},"4":{"en":"₹400"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(0.4A = 0.5N \\Rightarrow A = 1.25N\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1.25N - 200}{N} = \\frac{3}{4} \\Rightarrow 5N - 800 = 3N\\)<br>₹\\(2N = 800 \\Rightarrow N = \\boxed{400}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹400.</b>","hi":"\\(0.4A = 0.5N \\Rightarrow A = 1.25N\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1.25N - 200}{N} = \\frac{3}{4} \\Rightarrow 5N - 800 = 3N\\)<br>₹\\(2N = 800 \\Rightarrow N = \\boxed{400}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹400 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000074438","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"Three partners, P, Q, and R, have established a business venture. P invests three times the amount invested by Q, who, in turn, invests two-thirds of the amount of R. Given that the total annual profit earned from the business is ₹1,32,000, find the share of Q in the profit. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"तीन साझेदार P, Q और R ने एक व्यवसाय स्थापित किया है। P, Q द्वारा निवेशित राशि का तीन गुना निवेश करता है, जो बदले में R की राशि का दो-तिहाई निवेश करता है। यदि व्यवसाय से कुल वार्षिक लाभ ₹1,32,000 है, तो लाभ में Q का हिस्सा ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹20,000"},"2":{"en":"₹48,000"},"3":{"en":"₹36,000"},"4":{"en":"₹24,000"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let Q invest \\(2x\\); then P \\(= 6x\\) and R \\(= 3x\\)<br>Ratio \\(P : Q : R = 6 : 2 : 3\\), total parts \\(= 11\\)<br>Q's share ₹\\(= \\frac{2}{11} \\times 1{,}32{,}000 = \\boxed{24{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹24,000.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए Q ने \\(2x\\) निवेश किया; तब P \\(= 6x\\) और R \\(= 3x\\)<br>अनुपात \\(P : Q : R = 6 : 2 : 3\\), कुल भाग \\(= 11\\)<br>Q का हिस्सा ₹\\(= \\frac{2}{11} \\times 1{,}32{,}000 = \\boxed{24{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹24,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000074439","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"During an election, 18% of the voters did not vote and 72 voters cast invalid votes. There were only two candidates. The winner obtained 51% of the total voters and won by 432 votes. Find the total number of voters. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक चुनाव में 18% मतदाताओं ने मत नहीं डाला और 72 मतदाताओं ने अवैध मत डाले। केवल दो उम्मीदवार थे। विजेता को कुल मतदाताओं के 51% मत मिले और वह 432 मतों से जीता। कुल मतदाताओं की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1200"},"2":{"en":"2400"},"3":{"en":"3200"},"4":{"en":"1800"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let total voters be \\(N\\); valid votes \\(= 0.82N - 72\\)<br>Winner \\(= 0.51N\\), loser \\(= 0.82N - 72 - 0.51N = 0.31N - 72\\)<br>\\(0.51N - (0.31N - 72) = 432 \\Rightarrow 0.2N + 72 = 432 \\Rightarrow 0.2N = 360\\)<br>\\(N = \\boxed{1800}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 1800.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए कुल मतदाता \\(N\\) हैं; वैध मत \\(= 0.82N - 72\\)<br>विजेता \\(= 0.51N\\), हारने वाला \\(= 0.31N - 72\\)<br>\\(0.51N - (0.31N - 72) = 432 \\Rightarrow 0.2N + 72 = 432 \\Rightarrow 0.2N = 360\\)<br>\\(N = \\boxed{1800}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 1800 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000074440","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A sum of money lent at simple interest amounts to 1.6 times the principal after a certain time. If the rate of interest is numerically double the time (in years), find the approximate annual rate of interest. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"साधारण ब्याज पर दी गई कोई धनराशि कुछ समय बाद मूलधन की 1.6 गुनी हो जाती है। यदि ब्याज दर संख्यात्मक रूप से समय (वर्षों में) की दोगुनी है, तो अनुमानित वार्षिक ब्याज दर ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9%"},"2":{"en":"11%"},"3":{"en":"16%"},"4":{"en":"14%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"SI \\(= 0.6P = \\frac{P \\times R \\times T}{100}\\) with \\(R = 2T\\)<br>\\(0.6 = \\frac{2T^2}{100} \\Rightarrow T^2 = 30 \\Rightarrow T = 5.48\\)<br>\\(R = 2 \\times 5.48 = 10.95\\% \\approx \\boxed{11\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 11%.</b>","hi":"SI \\(= 0.6P = \\frac{P \\times R \\times T}{100}\\) तथा \\(R = 2T\\)<br>\\(0.6 = \\frac{2T^2}{100} \\Rightarrow T^2 = 30 \\Rightarrow T = 5.48\\)<br>\\(R = 2 \\times 5.48 = 10.95\\% \\approx \\boxed{11\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 11% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000074441","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A regular hexagon is inscribed inside a circle of radius 14 cm. Find the area of the hexagon. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"14 cm त्रिज्या वाले एक वृत्त के भीतर एक सम षट्भुज अंतर्निहित है। षट्भुज का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(287\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²"},"2":{"en":"\\(259\\sqrt{7}\\) cm²"},"3":{"en":"\\(224\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²"},"4":{"en":"\\(294\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Side of the hexagon \\(= r = 14\\) cm<br>Area \\(= \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} r^2 = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 196\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{294\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(294\\sqrt{3}\\) cm².</b>","hi":"षट्भुज की भुजा \\(= r = 14\\) cm<br>क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} r^2 = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 196\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{294\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(294\\sqrt{3}\\) cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000074442","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"By selling an article for ₹720, a person incurs a loss of 10%. At what price should he sell it to gain 5%? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किसी वस्तु को ₹720 में बेचने पर एक व्यक्ति को 10% हानि होती है। 5% लाभ कमाने के लिए उसे इसे किस मूल्य पर बेचना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹750"},"2":{"en":"₹640"},"3":{"en":"₹840"},"4":{"en":"₹650"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"CP \\(= \\frac{720}{0.9} = 800\\)<br>SP for 5% gain \\(= 800 \\times 1.05\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{840}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹840.</b>","hi":"क्रय मूल्य \\(= \\frac{720}{0.9} = 800\\)<br>5% लाभ के लिए विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 800 \\times 1.05\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{840}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹840 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000074443","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A and B are the rivals. A is hired to do some work, A does the work while B destroys it. If A started at 2 pm and B started destroying at 3 pm, then the work finishes at 10 pm. Instead, if A started at 2 pm and B started destroying at 4 pm, then the work finishes at 6 pm. If B does not destroyed at all, find the time (in minutes) that A alone would take to complete the work. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A और B प्रतिद्वंद्वी हैं। A को कोई कार्य करने के लिए नियुक्त किया जाता है, A कार्य करता है जबकि B उसे नष्ट करता है। यदि A ने दोपहर 2 बजे शुरू किया और B ने दोपहर 3 बजे नष्ट करना शुरू किया, तो कार्य रात 10 बजे समाप्त होता है। इसके बजाय, यदि A ने दोपहर 2 बजे शुरू किया और B ने दोपहर 4 बजे नष्ट करना शुरू किया, तो कार्य शाम 6 बजे समाप्त होता है। यदि B बिल्कुल भी नष्ट न करे, तो A अकेले कार्य पूरा करने में कितना समय (मिनटों में) लेगा। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"120 minutes","hi":"120 मिनट"},"2":{"en":"224 minutes","hi":"224 मिनट"},"3":{"en":"144 minutes","hi":"144 मिनट"},"4":{"en":"184 minutes","hi":"184 मिनट"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let A's rate be \\(a\\) and B's destruction rate be \\(b\\) per hour<br>Case 1: \\(8a - 7b = 1\\); Case 2: \\(4a - 2b = 1\\)<br>From \\(8a - 7b = 4a - 2b\\): \\(4a = 5b \\Rightarrow b = 0.8a\\)<br>\\(4a - 1.6a = 1 \\Rightarrow 2.4a = 1 \\Rightarrow a = \\frac{1}{2.4}\\) per hour<br>Time \\(= 2.4\\) hours \\(= \\boxed{144\\ \\text{minutes}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 144 minutes.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए A की दर \\(a\\) और B की नष्ट करने की दर \\(b\\) प्रति घंटा है<br>स्थिति 1: \\(8a - 7b = 1\\); स्थिति 2: \\(4a - 2b = 1\\)<br>\\(8a - 7b = 4a - 2b\\) से: \\(4a = 5b \\Rightarrow b = 0.8a\\)<br>\\(4a - 1.6a = 1 \\Rightarrow 2.4a = 1 \\Rightarrow a = \\frac{1}{2.4}\\) प्रति घंटा<br>समय \\(= 2.4\\) घंटे \\(= \\boxed{144\\ \\text{minute}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 144 मिनट है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000074444","section":"MATH","topic":"Discount","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper marks his goods 40% above the cost price and offers a 15% discount on the marked price. Find the actual profit percentage. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक दुकानदार अपने माल को क्रय मूल्य से 40% अधिक अंकित करता है और अंकित मूल्य पर 15% छूट देता है। वास्तविक लाभ प्रतिशत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15%"},"2":{"en":"27%"},"3":{"en":"23%"},"4":{"en":"19%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let CP \\(= 100\\), MP \\(= 140\\)<br>SP \\(= 140 \\times 0.85 = 119\\)<br>Profit \\(= \\boxed{19\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 19%.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए क्रय मूल्य \\(= 100\\), अंकित मूल्य \\(= 140\\)<br>विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 140 \\times 0.85 = 119\\)<br>लाभ \\(= \\boxed{19\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 19% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000074445","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a cyclic quadrilateral ABCD, ∠A = (4x + 20)° and ∠C = (3x − 15)°. Find the value of x. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक चक्रीय चतुर्भुज ABCD में, ∠A = (4x + 20)° और ∠C = (3x − 15)° हैं। x का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18"},"2":{"en":"21"},"3":{"en":"27"},"4":{"en":"25"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral are supplementary<br>\\((4x + 20) + (3x - 15) = 180°\\)<br>\\(7x = 175 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{25}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 25.</b>","hi":"चक्रीय चतुर्भुज के सम्मुख कोण संपूरक होते हैं<br>\\((4x + 20) + (3x - 15) = 180°\\)<br>\\(7x = 175 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{25}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 25 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000074446","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta = \\frac{3}{2}\\), find the value of \\(\\tan\\theta + \\cot\\theta\\). [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta = \\frac{3}{2}\\) है, तो \\(\\tan\\theta + \\cot\\theta\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{8}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{8}{5}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(1 + 2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\frac{9}{4} \\Rightarrow \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\frac{5}{8}\\)<br>\\(\\tan\\theta + \\cot\\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{8}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{8}{5}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(1 + 2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\frac{9}{4} \\Rightarrow \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\frac{5}{8}\\)<br>\\(\\tan\\theta + \\cot\\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{8}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{8}{5}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000074447","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If x = 5 + 2√6, what is the value of x² + 1/x²? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि x = 5 + 2√6 है, तो x² + 1/x² का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"64"},"2":{"en":"87"},"3":{"en":"92"},"4":{"en":"98"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{x} = 5 - 2\\sqrt{6}\\), so \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 10\\)<br>\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 100 - 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{98}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 98.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{1}{x} = 5 - 2\\sqrt{6}\\), अतः \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 10\\)<br>\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 100 - 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{98}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 98 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000074448","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{2} = 1.414\\), then find the value of \\(\\frac{8\\sqrt{2} + 4}{\\sqrt{2}}\\). [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{2} = 1.414\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{8\\sqrt{2} + 4}{\\sqrt{2}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4.564"},"2":{"en":"8.452"},"3":{"en":"10.828"},"4":{"en":"12.456"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{8\\sqrt{2} + 4}{\\sqrt{2}} = 8 + \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}} = 8 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>\\(= 8 + 2(1.414)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{10.828}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 10.828.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{8\\sqrt{2} + 4}{\\sqrt{2}} = 8 + \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}} = 8 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>\\(= 8 + 2(1.414)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{10.828}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 10.828 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000074449","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle ABC, let D be any point on side AC. Points P, Q, X, and Y are the midpoints of AB, BC, AD, and DC, respectively. What is the ratio of the lengths PX and QY? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में, मान लीजिए D भुजा AC पर कोई बिंदु है। बिंदु P, Q, X और Y क्रमशः AB, BC, AD और DC के मध्यबिंदु हैं। लंबाइयों PX और QY का अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2:3"},"2":{"en":"1:1"},"3":{"en":"1:2"},"4":{"en":"3:2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In \\(\\triangle ABD\\), P and X are midpoints of AB and AD, so \\(PX = \\frac{BD}{2}\\)<br>In \\(\\triangle CBD\\), Q and Y are midpoints of CB and CD, so \\(QY = \\frac{BD}{2}\\)<br>Ratio \\(= \\boxed{1 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1:1.</b>","hi":"\\(\\triangle ABD\\) में P और X, AB तथा AD के मध्यबिंदु हैं, अतः \\(PX = \\frac{BD}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\triangle CBD\\) में Q और Y, CB तथा CD के मध्यबिंदु हैं, अतः \\(QY = \\frac{BD}{2}\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= \\boxed{1 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1:1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000074450","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"The circumference of a circle is 100π cm. A chord in this circle has a length of 60 cm. What is the distance of this chord from the centre? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक वृत्त की परिधि 100π cm है। इस वृत्त में एक जीवा की लंबाई 60 cm है। केंद्र से इस जीवा की दूरी क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 cm"},"2":{"en":"40 cm"},"3":{"en":"60 cm"},"4":{"en":"80 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(2\\pi r = 100\\pi \\Rightarrow r = 50\\) cm<br>Half chord \\(= 30\\) cm<br>Distance \\(= \\sqrt{50^2 - 30^2} = \\sqrt{1600} = \\boxed{40\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 40 cm.</b>","hi":"\\(2\\pi r = 100\\pi \\Rightarrow r = 50\\) cm<br>आधी जीवा \\(= 30\\) cm<br>दूरी \\(= \\sqrt{50^2 - 30^2} = \\sqrt{1600} = \\boxed{40\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 40 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000074451","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"AT is a tangent to a circle at A, and ABC is an inscribed triangle with BC as a chord. If the angle between the tangent and chord AC is ∠CAT = 50°, what is the inscribed angle ∠ABC? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"AT एक वृत्त पर A बिंदु पर स्पर्श रेखा है और ABC एक अंतर्निहित त्रिभुज है जिसमें BC एक जीवा है। यदि स्पर्श रेखा और जीवा AC के बीच का कोण ∠CAT = 50° है, तो अंतर्निहित कोण ∠ABC क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30°"},"2":{"en":"50°"},"3":{"en":"70°"},"4":{"en":"90°"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"By the alternate segment theorem, the angle between a tangent and a chord equals the angle in the alternate segment<br>\\(\\angle ABC = \\angle CAT\\)<br>\\(\\angle ABC = \\boxed{50°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 50°.</b>","hi":"एकांतर वृत्तखंड प्रमेय के अनुसार स्पर्श रेखा और जीवा के बीच का कोण एकांतर वृत्तखंड के कोण के बराबर होता है<br>\\(\\angle ABC = \\angle CAT\\)<br>\\(\\angle ABC = \\boxed{50°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 50° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000074452","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two circles of radii 6 cm and 4 cm have their centres 20 cm apart. The transverse common tangent intersects the line joining the centres at point P. Find the distance of P from the centre of the larger circle. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"6 cm और 4 cm त्रिज्या वाले दो वृत्तों के केंद्र 20 cm की दूरी पर हैं। तिर्यक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा केंद्रों को जोड़ने वाली रेखा को बिंदु P पर प्रतिच्छेद करती है। बड़े वृत्त के केंद्र से P की दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 cm"},"2":{"en":"10 cm"},"3":{"en":"12 cm"},"4":{"en":"14 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"P divides the line of centres externally in the ratio of the radii, \\(6 : 4\\)<br>Distance from the larger centre \\(= \\frac{6}{6 - 4} \\times 20\\)… using the internal point for transverse tangents: \\(\\frac{6}{10} \\times 20\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{12\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12 cm.</b>","hi":"P केंद्र रेखा को त्रिज्याओं \\(6 : 4\\) के अनुपात में विभाजित करता है<br>बड़े केंद्र से दूरी \\(= \\frac{6}{10} \\times 20\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{12\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000074453","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"Two circles have radii in the ratio 3 : 5. The arc of the smaller circle subtends 75° at its centre, and the arc of the larger circle subtends 45° at its centre. What is the ratio of their arc lengths (smaller : larger)? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो वृत्तों की त्रिज्याएँ 3 : 5 के अनुपात में हैं। छोटे वृत्त का चाप उसके केंद्र पर 75° और बड़े वृत्त का चाप उसके केंद्र पर 45° का कोण अंतरित करता है। उनके चापों की लंबाइयों का अनुपात (छोटा : बड़ा) क्या है? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3:5"},"2":{"en":"5:3"},"3":{"en":"1:1"},"4":{"en":"2:3"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Arc \\(= \\frac{\\theta}{360°} \\times 2\\pi r\\)<br>Smaller \\(\\propto 3 \\times 75 = 225\\), larger \\(\\propto 5 \\times 45 = 225\\)<br>Ratio \\(= \\boxed{1 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1:1.</b>","hi":"चाप \\(= \\frac{\\theta}{360°} \\times 2\\pi r\\)<br>छोटा \\(\\propto 3 \\times 75 = 225\\), बड़ा \\(\\propto 5 \\times 45 = 225\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= \\boxed{1 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1:1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000074454","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 8\\), then find the value of \\(x^4 + \\frac{1}{x^4}\\). [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 8\\) है, तो \\(x^4 + \\frac{1}{x^4}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3846"},"2":{"en":"3844"},"3":{"en":"3842"},"4":{"en":"3840"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 64 - 2 = 62\\)<br>\\(x^4 + \\frac{1}{x^4} = 62^2 - 2 = 3844 - 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3842}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3842.</b>","hi":"\\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 64 - 2 = 62\\)<br>\\(x^4 + \\frac{1}{x^4} = 62^2 - 2 = 3844 - 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3842}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3842 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000074455","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"Two varieties of wheat costing ₹36/kg and ₹54/kg are mixed to obtain a mixture worth ₹45/kg. If 6 kg of the cheaper wheat are added to the mixture, the ratio of cheaper wheat to costlier wheat becomes 3:2. Find the original quantity of costlier wheat. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"₹36/kg और ₹54/kg लागत वाले गेहूँ की दो किस्में ₹45/kg मूल्य का मिश्रण प्राप्त करने के लिए मिलाई जाती हैं। यदि मिश्रण में 6 kg सस्ता गेहूँ और मिला दिया जाए, तो सस्ते गेहूँ और महँगे गेहूँ का अनुपात 3:2 हो जाता है। महँगे गेहूँ की मूल मात्रा ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 kg"},"2":{"en":"12 kg"},"3":{"en":"14 kg"},"4":{"en":"6 kg"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Alligation: cheaper : costlier \\(= (54 - 45) : (45 - 36) = 9 : 9 = 1 : 1\\)<br>So both quantities were equal, say \\(x\\) kg each<br>\\(\\frac{x + 6}{x} = \\frac{3}{2} \\Rightarrow 2x + 12 = 3x \\Rightarrow x = 12\\)<br>Costlier wheat \\(= \\boxed{12\\ \\text{kg}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 12 kg.</b>","hi":"मिश्रण नियम: सस्ता : महँगा \\(= (54 - 45) : (45 - 36) = 9 : 9 = 1 : 1\\)<br>अतः दोनों मात्राएँ बराबर थीं, मान लीजिए \\(x\\) kg प्रत्येक<br>\\(\\frac{x + 6}{x} = \\frac{3}{2} \\Rightarrow 2x + 12 = 3x \\Rightarrow x = 12\\)<br>महँगा गेहूँ \\(= \\boxed{12\\ \\text{kg}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 12 kg है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000074456","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correctly spelt word.<br><br>You must always _________ your luggage before the flight. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"recieve"},"2":{"en":"receive"},"3":{"en":"receeve"},"4":{"en":"receve"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Receive (प्राप्त करना) = to get or accept something given or sent.</b><br>Rule: 'i' before 'e' except after 'c' – so it is re-c-<b>ei</b>-ve.<br><b>recieve</b> – 'ie' after 'c'<br><b>receeve</b> – 'ee' in place of 'ei'<br><b>receve</b> – 'i' missing<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): receive.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000074457","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the correct spelling of the word? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Disenfranchaisement"},"2":{"en":"Desenfranchisement"},"3":{"en":"Disinfranchisement"},"4":{"en":"Disenfranchisement"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Disenfranchisement (मताधिकार से वंचित करना) = the act of depriving someone of a right, especially the right to vote.</b><br>Spelling: dis-en-franch-ise-ment.<br><b>Disenfranchaisement</b> – extra 'a' (-chai-)<br><b>Desenfranchisement</b> – 'De' in place of 'Dis'<br><b>Disinfranchisement</b> – 'in' in place of 'en'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Disenfranchisement.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000074458","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a one-word substitution for a life-sized model of the human body used to display clothes? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mannequin"},"2":{"en":"Sculptor"},"3":{"en":"Tailor"},"4":{"en":"Designer"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Mannequin (पुतला) = a life-size model of the human body used to display clothes in shops.</b><br><b>Sculptor (मूर्तिकार)</b> = an artist who makes sculptures<br><b>Tailor (दर्ज़ी)</b> = a person who makes or alters clothes<br><b>Designer (डिज़ाइनर)</b> = a person who plans the look of clothes or objects<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Mannequin.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000074459","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br><br>With the awarding of the 2024 Nobel Prize in Physics,<br>P. for their pioneering work in quantum materials,<br>Q. as scientists hailed the breakthrough for its potential applications in next-generation computing and renewable energy<br>R. the recipients sparked renewed interest in the study of exotic electronic properties,<br>S. while debates emerged over the accessibility of high-cost experimental setups required for further research. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PRQS"},"2":{"en":"PSQR"},"3":{"en":"RPQS"},"4":{"en":"QPRS"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: PRQS</b><br><b>P</b> 'for their pioneering work in quantum materials,' completes the opening phrase about the award.<br><b>R</b> gives the main clause: 'the recipients sparked renewed interest…'.<br><b>Q</b> 'as scientists hailed the breakthrough…' adds the reaction.<br><b>S</b> 'while debates emerged…' gives the contrast and ends with a full stop.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): PRQS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000074460","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br><br>The geopolitical landscape<br>P. necessitating strategic alliances and diplomatic interventions<br>Q. has been reshaped by emerging superpowers,<br>R. as nations navigate complex economic and military rivalries<br>S. to maintain regional stability and global influence [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QPRS"},"2":{"en":"SRPQ"},"3":{"en":"RSPQ"},"4":{"en":"SQPR"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QPRS</b><br><b>Q</b> gives the verb for 'The geopolitical landscape': 'has been reshaped by emerging superpowers,'.<br><b>P</b> 'necessitating strategic alliances and diplomatic interventions' shows the result.<br><b>R</b> 'as nations navigate complex … rivalries' gives the situation.<br><b>S</b> 'to maintain regional stability and global influence' states the purpose and ends the sentence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): QPRS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000074461","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?</b><br><br>1. Fossil evidence suggests that whales evolved from land-dwelling ancestors that gradually adapted to aquatic life.<br>2. Over millions of years, their limbs transformed into flippers, and their nostrils shifted to the top of their heads, forming blowholes.<br>3. This transformation is considered one of the most remarkable examples of evolutionary adaptation in the animal kingdom.<br>4. The discovery of transitional fossils, such as <i>Ambulocetus</i>, provides crucial insights into this evolutionary shift.<br>5. The ancestors of modern whales were hoofed mammals that once roamed the land before returning to the sea. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-4-3-5-1"},"2":{"en":"2-4-5-1-3"},"3":{"en":"4-2-1-3-5"},"4":{"en":"5-1-2-4-3"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 5-1-2-4-3</b><br><b>5</b> opens with the ancestors of whales – hoofed land mammals.<br><b>1</b> adds fossil evidence of their gradual adaptation to water.<br><b>2</b> 'their limbs transformed…' describes the changes.<br><b>4</b> 'this evolutionary shift' refers to the changes in 2.<br><b>3</b> 'This transformation is considered…' concludes the paragraph.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 5-1-2-4-3.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000074462","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Phrasal Verbs","question":{"en":"Improve the sentence using the correct phrasal verb of the underlined words.<br><br>We must <u>bring out</u> a solution to this problem quickly. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"bring up"},"2":{"en":"bring over"},"3":{"en":"bring about"},"4":{"en":"bring out"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Bring about (लाना, उत्पन्न करना) = to cause something to happen.</b><br>A solution is something we must make happen, so 'bring about' fits.<br>Correct sentence: We must <b>bring about</b> a solution to this problem quickly.<br><b>Bring up (उठाना; पालना)</b> = to raise a topic or to rear a child<br><b>Bring over (साथ लाना)</b> = to bring someone or something to a place<br><b>Bring out (प्रकाशित करना; उजागर करना)</b> = to publish or reveal<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): bring about.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000074463","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br><br>\"The voters know very little about Mr. Singh, but he’s a <b>dark horse</b> and I think he’ll win the election.\" [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A dishonest candidate who hides the truth"},"2":{"en":"A person who is not expected to succeed but ends up doing well"},"3":{"en":"A candidate who is very experienced and well-known"},"4":{"en":"A person who refuses to take part in the competition"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Dark horse (छुपा रुस्तम) = a little-known person who unexpectedly succeeds.</b><br>Voters know little about Mr. Singh, yet he may win.<br>Example: The newcomer proved a dark horse and won the title.<br>Dishonest candidate (बेईमान उम्मीदवार) – the idiom says nothing about honesty<br>Very experienced and well-known (अनुभवी व प्रसिद्ध) – opposite<br>Refuses to take part (भाग न लेना) – unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A person who is not expected to succeed but ends up doing well.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000074464","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Which of the following options is NOT one of the meanings of the homonym 'impertinent'? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Irrelevant or not related to the matter at hand"},"2":{"en":"Inappropriate in a given context"},"3":{"en":"Rude or disrespectful, especially towards someone older or in authority"},"4":{"en":"Very eager or passionate about a subject"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Impertinent (धृष्ट; असंगत) has more than one meaning.</b><br>Rude or disrespectful: 'an impertinent remark to the teacher' – valid<br>Not suitable to the situation: 'impertinent behaviour at a funeral' – valid<br>Not relevant (formal, legal use): 'impertinent evidence' – valid<br>'Very eager or passionate about a subject' is not a meaning of 'impertinent'.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Very eager or passionate about a subject.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000074465","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>\"Normal science, the activity in which most scientists inevitably spend almost all their time, is based on the assumption that the scientific community knows what the world is like. Scientists take great pains to defend that assumption, often restricting their vision to the phenomena that the existing paradigm has defined as relevant. When research proceeds in this fashion, findings tend to be incremental, reinforcing the established framework rather than challenging it. Yet, over time, anomalies—empirical observations that cannot be explained within the current paradigm—accumulate. Initially, these anomalies are dismissed as errors or as problems to be solved within the existing theoretical structure. However, as these anomalies grow in number and significance, they begin to erode confidence in the prevailing paradigm.<br><br>The resolution of such crises is not a straightforward process of falsification, as Popper might suggest, but rather a transformation in the very way scientists see the world. Scientific revolutions occur when a new paradigm emerges—one that is not merely an extension of the old but a fundamental reconceptualization of reality. This shift is not purely logical or empirical; it involves a radical change in perspective, akin to a gestalt switch. The Copernican Revolution, for example, did not merely adjust astronomical calculations; it redefined the very framework through which celestial motion was understood. Similarly, Einstein’s theory of relativity did not just modify Newtonian mechanics but replaced its foundational assumptions about space and time.<br><br><br>What is the best synonym for <b>“incommensurable”</b> in the sentence:<br><br>“What makes these revolutions particularly striking is that competing paradigms are often incommensurable.” [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Comparable"},"2":{"en":"Parallel"},"3":{"en":"Disjointed"},"4":{"en":"Irreconcilable"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…competing paradigms are often incommensurable.\"</i><br><b>Incommensurable (अतुलनीय, असंगत)</b> = having no common standard; impossible to bring into agreement. The passage says a new paradigm replaces the old, not extends it.<br><b>Irreconcilable (असमाधेय, जिनका मेल न हो)</b> ✔<br><b>Comparable (तुलनीय)</b> – antonym<br><b>Parallel (समानांतर)</b> – similar, side by side; not the sense<br><b>Disjointed (असंबद्ध)</b> = badly connected – describes poor organisation, not incompatibility<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Irreconcilable.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000074466","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>\"Normal science, the activity in which most scientists inevitably spend almost all their time, is based on the assumption that the scientific community knows what the world is like. Scientists take great pains to defend that assumption, often restricting their vision to the phenomena that the existing paradigm has defined as relevant. When research proceeds in this fashion, findings tend to be incremental, reinforcing the established framework rather than challenging it. Yet, over time, anomalies—empirical observations that cannot be explained within the current paradigm—accumulate. Initially, these anomalies are dismissed as errors or as problems to be solved within the existing theoretical structure. However, as these anomalies grow in number and significance, they begin to erode confidence in the prevailing paradigm.<br><br>The resolution of such crises is not a straightforward process of falsification, as Popper might suggest, but rather a transformation in the very way scientists see the world. Scientific revolutions occur when a new paradigm emerges—one that is not merely an extension of the old but a fundamental reconceptualization of reality. This shift is not purely logical or empirical; it involves a radical change in perspective, akin to a gestalt switch. The Copernican Revolution, for example, did not merely adjust astronomical calculations; it redefined the very framework through which celestial motion was understood. Similarly, Einstein’s theory of relativity did not just modify Newtonian mechanics but replaced its foundational assumptions about space and time.<br><br><br>What does the word <b>“gestalt switch”</b> imply in this context? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A subtle expansion of an existing model"},"2":{"en":"A shift from general to specific thinking"},"3":{"en":"A fundamental change in perception"},"4":{"en":"A reversal in cause-effect reasoning"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"This shift is not purely logical or empirical; it involves a radical change in perspective, akin to a gestalt switch.\"</i><br>A gestalt switch is a sudden change in how the whole picture is seen – a fundamental change in perception.<br>Option 1 – the passage says the new paradigm is 'not merely an extension'<br>Option 2 – general-to-specific thinking is not mentioned<br>Option 4 – cause-effect reversal is not mentioned<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): A fundamental change in perception.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000074467","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>\"Normal science, the activity in which most scientists inevitably spend almost all their time, is based on the assumption that the scientific community knows what the world is like. Scientists take great pains to defend that assumption, often restricting their vision to the phenomena that the existing paradigm has defined as relevant. When research proceeds in this fashion, findings tend to be incremental, reinforcing the established framework rather than challenging it. Yet, over time, anomalies—empirical observations that cannot be explained within the current paradigm—accumulate. Initially, these anomalies are dismissed as errors or as problems to be solved within the existing theoretical structure. However, as these anomalies grow in number and significance, they begin to erode confidence in the prevailing paradigm.<br><br>The resolution of such crises is not a straightforward process of falsification, as Popper might suggest, but rather a transformation in the very way scientists see the world. Scientific revolutions occur when a new paradigm emerges—one that is not merely an extension of the old but a fundamental reconceptualization of reality. This shift is not purely logical or empirical; it involves a radical change in perspective, akin to a gestalt switch. The Copernican Revolution, for example, did not merely adjust astronomical calculations; it redefined the very framework through which celestial motion was understood. Similarly, Einstein’s theory of relativity did not just modify Newtonian mechanics but replaced its foundational assumptions about space and time.<br><br><br>According to the passage, why do scientific revolutions represent a rupture rather than a continuation of prior science? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Because scientists abandon objectivity and turn to speculation"},"2":{"en":"Because new paradigms invalidate all previous findings"},"3":{"en":"Because competing paradigms redefine questions and methods, making continuity impossible"},"4":{"en":"Because scientists stop collecting empirical data"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…a new paradigm emerges—one that is not merely an extension of the old but a fundamental reconceptualization of reality… it redefined the very framework…\"</i><br>The new paradigm changes the framework itself, so there is no smooth continuation.<br>Option 1 – the passage does not say scientists give up objectivity<br>Option 2 – 'all previous findings' is too broad; frameworks change<br>Option 4 – stopping data collection is not mentioned<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Because competing paradigms redefine questions and methods, making continuity impossible.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000074468","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>\"Normal science, the activity in which most scientists inevitably spend almost all their time, is based on the assumption that the scientific community knows what the world is like. Scientists take great pains to defend that assumption, often restricting their vision to the phenomena that the existing paradigm has defined as relevant. When research proceeds in this fashion, findings tend to be incremental, reinforcing the established framework rather than challenging it. Yet, over time, anomalies—empirical observations that cannot be explained within the current paradigm—accumulate. Initially, these anomalies are dismissed as errors or as problems to be solved within the existing theoretical structure. However, as these anomalies grow in number and significance, they begin to erode confidence in the prevailing paradigm.<br><br>The resolution of such crises is not a straightforward process of falsification, as Popper might suggest, but rather a transformation in the very way scientists see the world. Scientific revolutions occur when a new paradigm emerges—one that is not merely an extension of the old but a fundamental reconceptualization of reality. This shift is not purely logical or empirical; it involves a radical change in perspective, akin to a gestalt switch. The Copernican Revolution, for example, did not merely adjust astronomical calculations; it redefined the very framework through which celestial motion was understood. Similarly, Einstein’s theory of relativity did not just modify Newtonian mechanics but replaced its foundational assumptions about space and time.<br><br><br><b>Identify the voice used in the sentence:</b><br><br>\"Anomalies are dismissed as errors or as problems to be solved within the existing theoretical structure.\" [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Active voice"},"2":{"en":"Passive voice"},"3":{"en":"Middle voice"},"4":{"en":"Reflexive voice"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…these anomalies are dismissed as errors or as problems to be solved…\"</i><br>'are dismissed' = be + V3, and the subject 'anomalies' receives the action. This is the passive voice.<br>Active voice – the subject would perform the action<br>Middle voice – subject acts on itself without a passive form ('The door opened')<br>Reflexive voice – uses a reflexive pronoun ('himself')<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Passive voice.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000074469","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>\"Normal science, the activity in which most scientists inevitably spend almost all their time, is based on the assumption that the scientific community knows what the world is like. Scientists take great pains to defend that assumption, often restricting their vision to the phenomena that the existing paradigm has defined as relevant. When research proceeds in this fashion, findings tend to be incremental, reinforcing the established framework rather than challenging it. Yet, over time, anomalies—empirical observations that cannot be explained within the current paradigm—accumulate. Initially, these anomalies are dismissed as errors or as problems to be solved within the existing theoretical structure. However, as these anomalies grow in number and significance, they begin to erode confidence in the prevailing paradigm.<br><br>The resolution of such crises is not a straightforward process of falsification, as Popper might suggest, but rather a transformation in the very way scientists see the world. Scientific revolutions occur when a new paradigm emerges—one that is not merely an extension of the old but a fundamental reconceptualization of reality. This shift is not purely logical or empirical; it involves a radical change in perspective, akin to a gestalt switch. The Copernican Revolution, for example, did not merely adjust astronomical calculations; it redefined the very framework through which celestial motion was understood. Similarly, Einstein’s theory of relativity did not just modify Newtonian mechanics but replaced its foundational assumptions about space and time.<br><br><br><b>What type of clause is used in the sentence:</b><br><br>“Yet, over time, anomalies that cannot be explained within the current paradigm accumulate.” [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Noun clause"},"2":{"en":"Adverbial clause"},"3":{"en":"Relative clause"},"4":{"en":"Independent clause"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…anomalies that cannot be explained within the current paradigm accumulate.\"</i><br>'that cannot be explained…' begins with the relative pronoun 'that' and describes the noun 'anomalies', so it is a relative (adjective) clause.<br>Noun clause – would act as subject or object<br>Adverbial clause – would modify the verb (time, reason, condition)<br>Independent clause – cannot stand alone; it depends on 'anomalies'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Relative clause.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000074470","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correctly spelt word.<br><br>The ritual had a distinctly _________ feel to it. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"hieratick"},"2":{"en":"hieretical"},"3":{"en":"hieratic"},"4":{"en":"hiearatic"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Hieratic (पुरोहिती, धार्मिक) = relating to priests; formal and solemn in a religious way.</b><br>A ritual with a priestly, solemn feel fits the sentence.<br><b>hieratick</b> – extra 'k' at the end<br><b>hieretical</b> – 'e' in place of 'a' and extra '-al'<br><b>hiearatic</b> – 'ea' in place of 'e'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): hieratic.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000074471","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br><b>Cried up</b> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ignored intentionally"},"2":{"en":"Exposed harshly"},"3":{"en":"Praised extravagantly"},"4":{"en":"Rejected summarily"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Cry up (बढ़ा-चढ़ाकर प्रशंसा करना) = to praise something highly, often more than it deserves.</b><br>Example: The film was cried up by critics before its release.<br>Ignored intentionally (जानबूझकर अनदेखा) – unrelated<br>Exposed harshly (कठोरता से उजागर) – opposite tone<br>Rejected summarily (तुरंत अस्वीकार) – opposite<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Praised extravagantly.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000074472","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br><b>Ride roughshod over</b> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Travel very quickly"},"2":{"en":"Disregard others’ feelings or rights"},"3":{"en":"Improve something drastically"},"4":{"en":"Face obstacles bravely"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Ride roughshod over (दूसरों की भावनाओं को रौंदना) = to act without caring about others' feelings or rights.</b><br>Example: The manager rode roughshod over the staff's objections.<br>Travel very quickly (तेज़ यात्रा) – literal reading<br>Improve drastically (भारी सुधार) – unrelated<br>Face obstacles bravely (साहस से सामना) – unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Disregard others’ feelings or rights.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000074473","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word<b>. Sententious</b> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Moralistic"},"2":{"en":"Terse"},"3":{"en":"Concise"},"4":{"en":"Unpretentious"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Sententious (उपदेशात्मक, आडंबरपूर्ण) = given to pompous moralising.</b><br><b>Unpretentious (सरल, आडंबरहीन)</b> = simple and modest ✔<br><b>Moralistic (नीतिवादी)</b> – synonym<br><b>Terse (संक्षिप्त)</b> = brief – an older sense of sententious (pithy), not opposite<br><b>Concise (संक्षिप्त)</b> – also close to the 'pithy' sense<br>More antonyms: modest, humble, plain-spoken.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Unpretentious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000074474","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word<b>. Jejune</b> [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Insipid"},"2":{"en":"Bland"},"3":{"en":"Dull"},"4":{"en":"Interesting"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Jejune (नीरस, फीका) = dull and uninteresting; naive.</b><br><b>Interesting (रोचक)</b> ✔<br><b>Insipid (फीका)</b> – synonym<br><b>Bland (नीरस)</b> – synonym<br><b>Dull (उबाऊ)</b> – synonym<br>More antonyms: stimulating, engaging, mature.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Interesting.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000074475","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"<b>Select the correct option:</b><br>Given the proliferation of misinformation, it becomes all the more imperative to ___ sources before dissemination. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ameliorate"},"2":{"en":"fabricate"},"3":{"en":"corroborate"},"4":{"en":"incriminate"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The verb must suit 'sources' and the aim of fighting misinformation.</b><br><b>Corroborate (पुष्टि करना)</b> = to confirm or verify – sources must be verified before spreading information.<br>Correct sentence: …it becomes all the more imperative to <b>corroborate</b> sources before dissemination.<br><b>Ameliorate (सुधारना)</b> = to make better – not used for sources<br><b>Fabricate (गढ़ना)</b> = to invent falsely – opposite purpose<br><b>Incriminate (दोषी ठहराना)</b> = to show someone guilty – unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): corroborate.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000074476","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Change the following from active to passive:</b><br>Did they approve your application? [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Is your application approved by them?"},"2":{"en":"Was your application approved by them?"},"3":{"en":"Has your application been approved by them?"},"4":{"en":"Had your application been approved by them?"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Did + S + V1 + O? → Was/Were + O + V3 + by + agent?</b><br>'your application' is singular, so 'Was'; 'they' → 'by them'.<br>Passive: <b>Was</b> your application <b>approved</b> by them?<br>Option 1 – simple present passive<br>Option 3 – present perfect passive<br>Option 4 – past perfect passive<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Was your application approved by them?.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000074477","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"<b>Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:</b><br>The professor recommended that each of the selected candidates (1)/ submit their thesis proposal by next Friday (2)/ failing which the slot would be offered to waitlisted scholars. (3)/ No error (4) [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'Each of + plural noun' is singular and takes a singular pronoun (his or her), not 'their'.</b><br>'submit' is correct (subjunctive after 'recommended that'), but 'their' in part (2) does not agree with 'each'.<br>Correct sentence: The professor recommended that each of the selected candidates submit <b>his or her</b> thesis proposal by next Friday…<br>Part (1) – 'each of the selected candidates' is correct<br>Part (3) – 'failing which' and 'would be offered' are correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): (2).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000074478","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:</b><br>The player is rumored to be considering early retirement after this season. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The player considers retiring early after the season, as rumored."},"2":{"en":"Early retirement is being rumored by the player."},"3":{"en":"Rumor has it that the player is considering early retirement."},"4":{"en":"It is rumored that the season caused early retirement."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'is rumored to be + V-ing' has no agent; the active form uses 'Rumor has it that…' with the continuous tense kept.</b><br>'to be considering' → 'is considering' in the 'that' clause.<br>Active: <b>Rumor has it that</b> the player is considering early retirement.<br>Option 1 – states it as fact; continuous tense lost<br>Option 2 – the player does not spread the rumour; meaning changed<br>Option 4 – still passive and changes the meaning<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Rumor has it that the player is considering early retirement.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000074479","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:</b><br>The evidence is believed to have been planted before the investigation began. [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The investigation believed that the evidence had been planted earlier."},"2":{"en":"It is believed that someone planted the evidence before the investigation began."},"3":{"en":"It is believed that the investigation planted the evidence."},"4":{"en":"Someone had believed the evidence to be planted before the investigation."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'to have been + V3' → a 'that' clause in active form with an indefinite agent ('someone') and the past tense.</b><br>'to have been planted' → 'someone planted'; 'is believed' is kept as 'It is believed'.<br>Active: It is believed that <b>someone planted</b> the evidence before the investigation began.<br>Option 1 – the investigation does not believe; meaning changed<br>Option 3 – the investigation did not plant the evidence<br>Option 4 – 'had believed' changes the tense, and 'to be planted' is still passive<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): It is believed that someone planted the evidence before the investigation began.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000074480","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"<b>A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech.</b><br>She said, “I hope he will arrive on time.” [SSC CGL 05/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She hoped he would arrive on time."},"2":{"en":"She said that I hope he will arrive on time."},"3":{"en":"She said that she hoped he arrived on time."},"4":{"en":"She said that she hoped he will arrive on time."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past reporting verb → 'hope' becomes 'hoped' and 'will' becomes 'would'; 'I' → 'she'.</b><br>The sentence can be reported compactly with the verb 'hoped'.<br>Indirect: She <b>hoped he would arrive</b> on time.<br>Option 2 – pronoun 'I' and tenses not changed<br>Option 3 – 'arrived' loses the future sense<br>Option 4 – 'will' not changed to 'would'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): She hoped he would arrive on time.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};